\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks stage strong comeback; Hungary's forint jumps\b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2022\par 11:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Oct 14 (Reuters) - Emerging market stocks made a strong comeback on Friday, cheered by China's stimulus promise and hopes of reversal of a controversial UK fiscal policy, while \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint jumped from record lows after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Riskier assets had taken a hit after hotter-than-expected U.S. consumer price inflation data on Thursday saw investors start to price in the possibility of a 100-basis-point hike by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 But the declines proved short-lived, with U.S. stocks closing up strongly on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "It seems like the market is starting to digest the fact that we will continue to be in an elevated inflation environment for the time being and for the foreseeable future so EM equities are tagging along," said \uc2 Cristian Maggio\uc2 , head of portfolio strategy at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Aiding the mood on Friday was the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's promise of stronger support for the economy and hopes that UK Prime Minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 's government will reverse parts of a 43-billion-pound package for unfunded tax cuts that rattled markets globally.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's index of emerging market shares gained 1.4%. Bourses from China to Africa jumped between 0.2% to 2.5% with Taiwan shares bolstered by a 4.3% rise in chipmaker \uc2 TSMC\uc2  after its quarterly profit jumped 80%.\par \par \uc2 On the week, however, the EM index is on track to lose about 3.4% - its sixth weekly loss in seven. Recession fears have gripped investors as central banks aggressively tighten monetary policy to control inflation.\par \par \uc2 EM-focussed asset manager \uc2 Ashmore\uc2  said its assets under management fell by $8 billion in the September quarter as rising geopolitical risks added to woes.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed. Most Asian units were in the red, with focus turning to China's Communist Party Congress which could see President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  win a third term.\par \par \uc2 South Africa's rand moved firmly away from May 2020 lows hit on Thursday, up 0.5% against a steady dollar.\par \par \uc2 HUNGARIAN SURGE\par \par \uc2 Hungary's forint bounced off record lows, rising as much as 3% before paring some the gains to trade at 418.21 per euro.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a new one-day deposit facility with an 18% interest rate and said it would provide the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to pay energy import bills until the end of the year, to aid the struggling forint.\par \par \uc2 "The overall question is whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Hungary is willing to tighten the screws of monetary policy from here, as recently they sounded more dovish than inflation outlook would suggest," Maggio said.\par \par \uc2 "It is very possible that they will have to continue, especially if the forint continues to depreciate."\par \par \uc2 The moves could pressure other regional central banks, especially Poland which is also in danger of prematurely calling an end to its rate hiking cycle, said \uc2 Abrdn\uc2 's portfolio manager Viktor Szabo. For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance in 2022, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance in 2022, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2OusNdX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\par \par \uc2 For TOP NEWS across emerging markets\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru and Marc Jones in London; Editing by Shailesh Kuber) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-14T10:32:57.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221014eiae01db2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
