\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Hungary's forint, stocks knocked by energy worries\b0\par\par\uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2022\par 22:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Ukraine suspends Russian oil flows to southern Europe \par     * Argentina industrial output up 6.9% in June vs a year ago\par     * Brazilian consumer prices drop sharply in July after tax\par cuts\par \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Susan Mathew\par     Aug 9 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint dropped 0.6% against the\par euro and Budapest-listed stocks tumbled 3% on Tuesday hit by oil\par supply worries, while most other emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made\par muted moves against a weaker dollar ahead of an inflation test. \par     Ukraine has suspended Russian oil flows to southern Europe\par since early this month because Western sanctions prevented it\par from receiving transit fees from Moscow, Russia's pipeline\par monopoly \f28 \uc2 \f2 Transneft\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday.\par     Russia normally supplies about 250,000 barrels per day via\par the southern leg of the Druzhba pipeline to Hungary, Slovakia\par and the Czech Republic.\par     The forint tracked its worst session in a month,\par while the Czech crown, which has been supported\par recently by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was little changed. \par     The main stock index in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was on course for its\par worst session in over three months, with energy group \f28 \uc2 \f2 MOL\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  down 4.2%.\par     "Even if this is resolved within days or a few weeks, it\par confirms or reiterates that central and eastern European\par countries will have a very difficult winter because of problems\par on the energy side," said Marek Drimal, lead CEEMEA strategist\par at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "Even if there are no massive problems with deliveries,\par energy prices are elevated and that will most likely impact\par production and purchasing power, and by extension widen current\par account deficits in CEE and be a fundamental drag on CEE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par performance," he said, expecting the forint to underperform into\par the year-end. \par     Other emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made small moves, ahead of\par U.S. inflation figures for July due on Wednesday. The headline\par number is seen dropping, but the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  is seen staying\par hawkish, with investors pricing in another 75 basis points hike\par in September.\par     Mexico's peso was down 0.1%, while Brazil's real\par  gave up early session gains to trade 0.4% lower. \par     Mexican annual inflation hit 22-year highs in July, rising\par faster than expected and fuelling expectations that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will raise the country's benchmark interest later this\par week. \par     "We forecast that inflation will only return to (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's) 2%-4% target range by late-2023 at the earliest," said\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jason Tuvey\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior emerging markets economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Capital\par Economics\f28 \uc2 \f2 , expecting the rate to end the year at 10%. \par     In Brazil, consumer prices fell more than expected in July,\par with the benchmark index recording its largest monthly drop\par ever, in the wake of a string of tax cuts and rate hikes.\par \par     Meanwhile, Argentina's industrial output grew 6.9% in June\par from a year ago in non-seasonally adjusted terms.\par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1945 GMT:\par     \par     \par     Stock indexes             Latest      Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets          1001.24              -0.05\par                                          \par  MSCI LatAm                     2207.65               0.13\par                                          \par  Brazil Bovespa               108670.71               0.25\par                                          \par  Mexico IPC                    47254.06              -0.21\par                                          \par  Chile IPSA                     5240.01              -0.39\par                                          \par  Argentina MerVal             122036.56             -1.546\par                                          \par  Colombia COLCAP                1322.45               -0.8\par                                          \par                                                           \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest      Daily % change\par  Brazil real                     5.1316              -0.37\par                                          \par  Mexico peso                    20.2636              -0.09\par                                          \par  Chile peso                       903.9               0.15\par                                          \par  Colombia peso                  4344.13              -0.86\par  Peru sol                        3.9175              -0.15\par                                          \par  Argentina peso                133.8300              -0.19\par  (interbank)                             \par                                          \par  Argentina peso                     288               1.39\par  (parallel)                              \par                                          \par  \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew and Anisha Sircar in Bengaluru;\par Editing by Susan 