\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Hungary's forint, stocks knocked by oil worries\b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2022\par 16:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Ukraine suspends Russian oil flows to southern Europe \par     * Hungary's forint on track for worst session in one month\par     * Hungary's energy group \f28 \uc2 \f2 MOL\f28 \uc2 \f2  slides 4.3%\par     * Mexican inflation spurs tightening bets\par \par     By Susan Mathew\par     Aug 9 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint dropped 0.8% against the\par euro and Budapest-listed stocks tumbled 2.3% on Tuesday hit by\par oil supply worries, while most other emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par made muted moves against a weaker dollar ahead of an inflation\par test. \par     Ukraine has suspended Russian oil flows to southern Europe\par since early this month because Western sanctions prevented it\par from receiving transit fees from Moscow, Russia's pipeline\par monopoly \f28 \uc2 \f2 Transneft\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday.\par     Russia normally supplies about 250,000 barrels per day via\par the southern leg of the Druzhba pipeline to Hungary, Slovakia\par and the Czech Republic.\par     The forint was on track for its worst session in a\par month, while the Czech crown, which has been supported\par recently by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was flat. \par     The main stock index in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was on course for its\par worst session in over three months, with energy group \f28 \uc2 \f2 MOL\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  down 4.3%.\par     "Even if this is resolved within days or a few weeks, it\par just confirms or reiterates that central and eastern European\par countries will have a very difficult winter because of problems\par on the energy side," said Marek Drimal, lead CEEMEA strategist\par at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "Even if there are no massive problems with deliveries,\par energy prices are elevated and that will most likely impact\par production and purchasing power, and by extension widen current\par account deficits in CEE and be a fundamental drag on CEE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par performance," he said, expecting the forint to underperform into\par the year-end. \par     The news lifted oil prices and aided \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of crude\par exporters such as the Colombian peso which rose 0.3%.\par \par     Other emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made small moves, ahead of\par U.S. inflation figures for July due on Wednesday. The headline\par number is seen dropping, but the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  is seen staying\par hawkish, with investors pricing in another 75 basis points hike\par in September.\par     Mexico's peso was flat, while Brazil's real\par gave up early session gains to trade 0.4% lower. \par     Mexican annual inflation hitting 22-year highs in July,\par rising faster than expected, fuelled expectations that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will raise the country's benchmark interest later\par this week. \par     "We forecast that inflation will only return to (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's) 2-4% target range by late-2023 at the earliest," said\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jason Tuvey\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior emerging markets economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Capital\par Economics\f28 \uc2 \f2 , expecting the rate to end the year at 10%. \par     In Brazil, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's latest inflation forecast\par strengthened the case that its aggressive monetary policy\par tightening may end soon.\par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1419 GMT:\par    Stock indexes            Latest    Daily %\par                                       change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets       1001.71    -0.01\par                                       \par  MSCI LatAm                  2205.09     0.01\par                                       \par  Brazil Bovespa            108331.61    -0.07\par                                       \par  Mexico IPC                 47236.50    -0.25\par                                       \par  Chile IPSA                  5238.92    -0.41\par                                       \par  Argentina MerVal               0.00        0\par                                       \par  Colombia COLCAP             1333.11        0\par                                       \par                                              \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2            Latest    Daily %\par                                       change\par  Brazil real                  5.1331    -0.40\par                                       \par  Mexico peso                 20.2453     0.00\par                                       \par  Chile peso                    897.9     0.82\par                                       \par  Colombia peso                4293.6     0.31\par  Peru sol                     3.9126    -0.03\par                                       \par  Argentina peso             133.8000    -0.17\par  (interbank)                          \par                                       \par  \par \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru; Editing by Susan\par Fenton)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-8-9T15:41:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220809ei8902t05\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
