\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-CEE MARKETS-Forint plunges, yields surge as Hungary hammered in global gloom\b0\par\par\uc2 977 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2022\par 16:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Recasts with new forint lows, jump in Hungarian government\par bond yields, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )\par     By Alan Charlish and Krisztina Than\par     WARSAW/BUDAPEST, July 6 (Reuters) - The forint\par plunged to new record lows on Wednesday while Hungarian\par government bond yields jumped, as the country's worsened risk\par profile and worries over the future of EU fund flows added to\par global fears of a recession.   \par      The Polish zloty also softened slightly as\par investors ditched risky assets amid worries about a sharp\par economic slowdown as energy prices surge, central banks hike\par interest rates and business sentiment worsens. But the forint\par was hammered, falling 2% on the day, and more than 11% so far\par this year, way underperforming the region.\par     "Positive news about an agreement over EU funds and impacts\par of fiscal and monetary tightening cooling domestic demand and\par improving the trade balance would be essential conditions to\par halt the underperformance of the HUF amidst the negative\par external risk environment," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note. \par     It said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (NBH) had limited room\par to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot market\par but could hike its 7.75% one-week deposit rate on Thursday, when\par the next tender is due.\par     "As the NBH may try to keep some munition for the remainder\par of the month, we see slightly more chances for a 50bp hike\par tomorrow but based on the June MPC communication we would not\par rule out a 100bp hike either to defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," it said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has not replied to emailed Reuters\par questions.\par     Hungarian bond yields surged 40-45 basis points at the short\par end and 20-25 basis points on longer-dated papers, with the\par 10-year yield hitting 8.7% on the secondary market, a trader\par said.\par     "Compared to what goes on in the forint market, this is\par still fairly moderate in terms of yield moves, what we can see\par is that investors try to buy into the market occasionally, as\par they are searching for the peak," the trader said, adding the\par market was waiting to see the next move from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \par     The forint was 2% weaker against the euro at 416 as of 1413\par GMT, sliding to fresh record lows during the day. According to\par the debt agency's fixing HUBONDFIX the yield on the 5-year bonds\par jumped 44 bps to 9.08%, and the 3-year hit even higher at 9.19%.\par     Meanwhile, markets have become more unsure about whether\par Poland will actually receive COVID-recovery funds from the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  after criticism of reforms meant to unblock the\par cash in Brussels.\par     The zloty was 0.3% weaker at 4.784, ahead of a rate-setting\par meeting on Thursday where analysts polled by Reuters expect the\par main rate to rise to 6.75% from 6.00%.\par     The Romanian leu, tightly controlled by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was flat after a rate-setting meeting at which the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  delivered its biggest interest rate hike\par in more than a decade, narrowing the borrowing cost gap with\par other states in the region as it raised its short-term inflation\par expectations. \par     Policymakers lifted the benchmark rate ROINTR=ECI by one\par percentage point to 4.75%, above average market expectations,\par their seventh consecutive monthly hike since October.\par     Markets in Prague were closed for a holiday.\par     \par                   CEE      SNAPSH   AT  1559 CET         \par                   MARKETS  OT                      \par                            \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     \par                            Latest  Previo  Daily   Change\par                                    us              \par                            bid     close   change  in\par                                                    2022\par  EURCZK  Czech    <EURCZK  24.781  24.759  -0.09%   +0.37\par  =       crown    =>            0       0               %\par  EURHUF  Hungary  <EURHUF  415.70  407.50  -1.97%  -11.14\par  =       forint   =>           00      00               %\par  EURPLN  Polish   <EURPLN  4.7840  4.7700  -0.29%  -4.03%\par  =       zloty    =>                               \par  EURRON  Romania  <EURRON  4.9426  4.9449   +0.05   +0.11\par  =       n leu    =>                            %       %\par  EURHRK  Croatia  <EURHRK  7.5190  7.5225   +0.05  -0.02%\par  =       n kuna   =>                            %  \par  EURRSD  Serbian  <EURRSD  117.37  117.40   +0.03   +0.18\par  =       dinar    =>           00      00       %       %\par          Note:    calculated from          1800          \par          daily                             CET     \par          change                                    \par                                                          \par                            Latest  Previo  Daily   Change\par                                 