\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Borrell argues that no \uc2 EU\uc2  country will evade sanctions despite Putin's efforts\b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS, 28 (EUROPA PRESS)\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2 's High Representative for Foreign Policy, \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 , defended Thursday that no EU member state will bypass sanctions despite attempts by Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  to receive payments for gas supplies in rubles.\par \par \uc2 "No member state will do anything that implies circumventing the sanctions and the contracts will be strictly fulfilled in the terms provided, where it says to pay in euros or dollars will be paid in euros or dollars," stressed the head of \uc2 EU\uc2  diplomacy at a press conference from Santiago de Chile, in the middle of a six-day tour of Latin America.\par \par \uc2 According to Borrell, there will be a solidarity response to the gas incident because "what happens to Poland and Bulgaria happens to the Union as a whole", and he also reiterated that the sanctions "will be respected".\par \par \uc2 After Russia has cut off gas supplies to Bulgaria and Poland for not paying in Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  has clarified Thursday that applying the two-step system required by the Kremlin to make gas payments is a violation of European sanctions against Moscow because it implies an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a condition \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  has announced it will abide by.\par \par \uc2 What does AMLO's electoral reform consist of?Two members of the Army deprived of their freedom in VallartaAMLO reaffirms the 4T before those who do not "betray the homeland".The Hungarian Government has confirmed that it will use the payment system implemented by Russia, despite the battery of sanctions imposed against Moscow for its military invasion of Ukraine. Budapest notes that it will do so "together with nine other nations" and that it "complies to the letter with the European sanctions policy."\par \par \uc2 PUTIN WANTS TO CONTINUE THIS WAR\par \par \uc2 On the progress of the war in Ukraine, the High Representative said that there are no signs that Russia will cease the offensive and, consequently, said that the \uc2 EU\uc2  will strengthen its response in the form of sanctions on Moscow and military assistance to Kiev.\par \par \uc2 "We are doing nothing but helping a country attacked without any justification, in the face of an aggressor who takes every opportunity to say that he wants to continue the war and increases the level of threat," he said.\par \par \uc2 Borrell said that the \uc2 EU\uc2  wants to promote diplomatic channels, but Russia "does not want to" and only seeks to "continue the war".\par \par \uc2 "The sanctions will continue and their effects will be felt," said the High Representative, who nevertheless admitted that measures against the import of Russian oil or gas do not have the necessary unanimity among the EU-27.\par \par \uc2 "It has not yet been possible to take them, which does not mean that they will not be reconsidered in the light of events", explained the former Spanish minister.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220428ei4s00c1o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
