\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-CEE MARKETS-Zloty pares losses on c.bank, finmin support\b0\par\par\uc2 787 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 17:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announcements)\par     By Alan Charlish\par     WARSAW, March 2 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty pared\par losses on Wednesday after both the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the finance\par ministry moved to support a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that had sunk to a 13-year\par low in a selloff sparked by Russia's invasion of Ukraine. \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Poland\f28 \uc2 \f2  (NBP) said it had sold foreign\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for zlotys for the second day in a row, while the\par finance ministry said it would exchange most foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par funds in the market rather than in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Russia's attack and the resulting raft of sanctions\par unleashed on Moscow had sent the zloty to its weakest level\par since February 2009, while the Hungarian forint hit a\par fresh record low.\par     "The NBP together with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be\par trying to do whatever it takes to strengthen the zloty to fight\par with inflation," said Mateusz Sutowicz, a financial market\par analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Millennium\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     At 1534 GMT, the zloty was 0.49% softer on the day versus\par the euro at 4.77. It had earlier been as weak as 4.8335.\par     The Hungarian forint was 1.16% weaker against the euro at\par 381.50. The Czech crown slid 1.12% to 25.72, while the\par Romanian leu was little changed at 4.9485.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday it was ready to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "at any moment" to ensure the stability of local\par financial markets, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was ready\par to react to excessive moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \par     Prior to the NBP's announcement on Wednesday, a Warsaw-based\par trader told Reuters that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been active in the\par market. "We've got the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that is hitting the bid from\par time to time," the trader said. "I wouldn't call it a very big\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but they occasionally call out."\par     Stocks were higher in Budapest and Warsaw, with Polish\par coking coal producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 JSW\f28 \uc2 \f2  rising 23% on the back of\par potential sanctions against coal imported from Russia.\par     On Tuesday, Polish Prime Minister Mateusz Morawiecki said\par Poland wanted the strongest possible sanctions to be introduced\par against Russia, including a ban on the import of coal.\par \par     \par     \par                    CEE      SNAPSHO   AT                      \par                    MARKETS  T        1634              \par                                      CET               \par                                                               \par                    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                     \par                    IES                                 \par           