\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Zloty slips further as focus shifts to U.S. stimulus\b0\par\par\uc2 752 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2021\par 11:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Alan Charlish\par     Jan 14 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty continued to\par slip on Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par further to weaken it, while dollar strength after a report about\par bigger-than-expected U.S. stimulus provided a risk for central\par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     President-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Joe Biden\f28 \uc2 \f2  is due to outline his economic\par plans later on Thursday, and CNN reported that he could spend $2\par trillion in stimulus, well above market expectations. U.S.\par treasury yields rose on the news, boosting the dollar.\par     "Given the strong negative correlation between CEE\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the euro/dollar, this can be a game-changer, at\par least temporarily," said Piotr Poplawski, senior economist at\par ING in Warsaw, referring to the Biden press conference.\par     At 0956 GMT, the zloty was 0.10% weaker against the euro at\par 4.5416, after having slipped as much as 0.4% on Wednesday\par afternoon after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept its key interest rate at\par 0.1% but indicated further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par markets to weaken it are possible.\par     Asked about the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in an\par interview published on Thursday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par (NBH)Deputy Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barnabas Virag\f28 \uc2 \f2  told news website\par portfolio.hu that it "did not want to participate in any\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war."\par     Virag also said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should stick to its\par cautious monetary policy stance.\par     The Hungarian forint was 0.24% stronger against\par the euro at 359.70. "...The relative strength of the HUF vs the\par PLN, seen since end-December, could remain," Erste said in a\par note, referring to Virag's comments.\par     The Czech crown softened 0.1% to 26.1840.\par     Stocks inched higher amid news of the Biden stimulus plan.\par The main indices in Prague, Budapest and Warsaw\par  were up 0.1-0.6%\par     "At the beginning of the year, generally, not too much is\par happening on the stock markets; we have consolidation. There are\par expectations about the stimulus from Biden which is supposed to\par happen," said DM BOS analyst Konrad Ryczko.\par     \par                    CEE      SNAPSHO   AT                      \par                    MARKETS  T        1056              \par                                      CET               \par                                                               \par                    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                     \par                    IES                                 \par                             Latest   Previou  Daily    Change\par                                      s                 \par                             bid      close    change   in 2021\par  EURCZK  Czech     <EURCZK  26.1840  26.1590   -0.10%   +0.17%\par  =       crown     =>                                