\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  ease, \uc2 Hungarian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  meeting in focus\b0\par\par\uc2 851 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2020\par 10:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BUCHAREST, April 28 (Reuters) - Central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par edged lower against the euro in early trade on Tuesday as a new\par fall in oil prices tempered risk appetite, while in Hungary\par investors were waiting to see the scope of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par planned asset-purchasing programme.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Hungary\f28 \uc2 \f2  holds a rate-setting meeting\par later on Tuesday. The bank is expected to hold its key rates\par after a surprise increase in lending rates early this month, a\par Reuters poll showed.\par     But policymakers are expected to detail the scale and terms\par of the asset-purchasing programme it signalled earlier this\par month.\par     "If the statement stresses that the asset-purchasing\par programme is being introduced in order to help stabilize the\par government bond market, and that they will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  only when\par specific conditions are met, then the exchange rate of the\par forint might strengthen further" an Equilor research note said.\par     ING analysts agreed. "We expect the NBH to announce\par conditional financial stability focused QE today, aiming to help\par the Hungarian bond market while not harming the forint," the\par bank said in a note.\par     The forint hit a record low near 370 versus the euro on\par April 1st and regained some of its losses after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par offered a new one-week deposit for banks at 0.9% on Wednesday in\par a surprise move that analysts said amounted to an "implicit rate\par hike."\par     By 0750 GMT, the forint was trading at 355.5500 to\par the euro, down 0.1% on the day. \par     "The forint has been relatively stable and the Hungarian\par government managed to get good investor appetite for its new\par foreign bond issuance, which has set a more reassured tone in\par the market," Tatha Ghose of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  wrote in a note.\par     "We do not expect any change to conventional monetary policy\par in coming months, but we are likely to see a continuous stream\par of micro \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in lending, regulation and debt relief,"\par he added.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has sold 2 billion euros worth of 6-year and 12-year\par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds to cover a surge in financing needs due\par to the coronavirus pandemic.\par     Elsewhere, the Czech crown was flat and the Polish\par zloty and the Romanian leu each traded 0.1%\par lower versus the euro.\par     Romania's consolidated budget deficit widened to 1.7% of\par gross domestic product in the first quarter compared with a gap\par of 0.7% at the end of February as the coronavirus outbreak led\par to a plunge in revenue, the finance ministry said.\par     With the deficit above \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  limits even before the new\par coronavirus outbreak, Romanian assets and ratings have been\par under pressure.\par     Analysts said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would likely tread water ahead of\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meetings later\par this week.\par     Stock markets were mixed. The blue chip index in Prague\par  was flat while Budapest was up 0.3% by 0757 GMT.\par Warsaw's was up0.8% and Bucharest's up 0.4%.\par     \par             CEE       SNAPSHO   AT                      \par             MARKETS   T        0957              \par                                CET               \par                       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            \par                       IES                        \par                       Latest   Previou  Daily    Change\par                                s                 \par                       bid      close    change   in 2020\par  Czech      <EURCZK=  27.3000  27.3010   +0.00%   -6.84%\par  crown      >                                    \par  Hungary    <EURHUF=  355.550  355.200   -0.10%   -6.86%\par  forint     >               0        0           \par  Polish     <EURPLN=   4.5370   4.5330   -0.09%   -6.18%\par  zloty      >                                    \par  Romanian   <EURRON=   4.8445   4.8410   -0.07%   -1.16%\par  leu        >                                    \par  Croatian   <EURHRK=   7.5510   7.5527   +0.02%   -1.40%\par  kuna       >                                    \par  Serbian    <EURRSD=  117.620  117.680   +0.05%   -0.04%\par  dinar      >               0        0           \par  Note:      calculated from             1800            \par  daily                                  CET      \par  change                                          \par                                                         \par                       Latest   Previou  Daily    Change\par                                s                 \par                                close    change   in 2020\par  Prague                858.91  859.330   -0.05%  -23.01%\par                                      0           \par  Budapest             33292.1  33196.8   +0.29%  -27.76%\par                             8        5           \par  Warsaw               1604.09  1591.97   +0.76%  -2