\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Forint firms to 4-week high on hawkish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2 , ratings outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 941 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2020\par 12:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Anita Komuves\par     Feb 17 (Reuters) - The forint firmed to a new\par four-week high on Monday following a hawkish verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (NBH) last week and a change in\par the outlook on the country's debt to positive by rating agency\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard and Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The forint rose 0.33% to 334.80 versus the euro,\par in tandem with the Czech crown, which gained 0.35% to\par the euro, both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  supported by recent hawkish messages\par from local monetary policy makers.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly hiked rates earlier this\par month, which boosted the crown. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has gained 2.6% to\par the euro this year.\par     Higher-than-expected inflation data and low GDP growth,\par published on Friday, further strengthened the crown according to\par analysts. \par     "With the inflation that high, the likelihood of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cutting rates this year could be smaller," analysts at\par Erste's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ceska Sporitelna\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said in a note.\par     Hungary's ultra-dovish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday pledged to\par deploy its full monetary arsenal to rein in higher-than-expected\par inflation. The NBH has kept its benchmark rate at a record low\par of 0.9% since 2016.\par     "The HUF reacted positively with Vice Governor Nagy\par announcing that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to 'use all available\par tools to achieve the inflation target', including rates and\par liquidity management," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said in a note.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will focus on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps tool until the\par March 24 decision, when forecasts are updated in the new\par Inflation Report."\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will hold its weekly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap tender\par providing forint liquidity for commercial banks later on Monday\par  which will be closely eyed by market players. The bank\par offered 320 million euros worth of swaps to banks. Results will\par be published after 1400 GMT.\par     S&P Global Ratings on Friday revised its outlook on Hungary\par to positive from stable on strong economic growth prospects and\par as macroeconomic imbalances remain contained. Fitch, however,\par affirmed Hungary's long-term foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issuer default\par rating at 'BBB', with a stable outlook.\par     Markets are reacting to the positive decision by S&P,\par dealers in Budapest said, adding that the NBH's comments last\par week were still the main factor boosting the forint. \par     Stock markets gained, as nerves over the coronavirus have\par calmed to some extent following stimulus measure from China.\par Budapest led gains by rising 0.8%. The Polish stock market\par  rose 0.2%.\par     The zloty, however, traded 0.1% lower to the euro\par after inflation rose faster than expected in January, according\par to data published on Friday.\par     Earlier this month, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  head \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adam Glapinski\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par reiterated his long-held view that the bank's main interest rate\par will most likely stay at a record low of 1.5% until the end of\par the current rate-setting panel's term in 2022.\par     "Governor Glapinski continued to guide towards rates\par stability until 2022 but the overshooting inflation is likely to\par allow for the hawkish MPC members to be vocal about delivering a\par hike; however, reaching a majority unless Glapinski changes\par sides will remain difficult," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note on\par Friday.\par \par                    CEE      SNAPSHO   AT                      \par                    MARKETS  T        1036              \par                                      CET               \par                             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            \par                             IES                        \par                             Latest   Previou  Daily    Change\par                                      s                 \par                             bid      close    change   in 2020\par  EURCZK  Czech     <EURCZK  24.7880  24.8740   +0.35%   +2.60%\par  =       crown     =>                                  \par  EURHUF  Hungary   <EURHUF  334.800  335.900   +0.33%   -1.09%\par  =       forint    =>             0        0           \par  EURPLN  Polish    <EURPLN   4.2520   4.2462   -0.14%   +0.10%\par  =       zloty     =>                                  \par  EURRON  Romanian  <EURRON   4.7735   4.7694   -0.09%   +0.31%\par  =       leu       =>                                  \par  EURHRK  Croatian  <EURHRK   7.4470   7.4505   +0.05%   -0.02%\par  =       kuna      =>                                  \par  EURRSD  Serbian   <EURRSD  117.500  117.510   +0.01% 