\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Forint paces  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains on robust GDP, cbank verbal  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2020\par 12:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Anita Komuves\par     Feb 14 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint paced\par regional gains on Friday morning, reacting to robust GDP growth\par and verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par against recent marked \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakening.\par     The forint was bid at 335.25 against the euro, 0.7% stronger\par on the day, after hitting a record low of 340.31 on Wednesday.\par     "Both markets and analysts consider remarks by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deputy governor as hawkish. But the words of the NBH will\par have to be followed by action," a dealer in Budapest said. \par     Dealers said markets paid close attention to NBH deputy\par governor Marton Nagy's remarks, which were delivered to\par investors in London earlier on Friday. Reuters confirmed the\par investor call took place but not what Nagy told participants.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Hungary\f28 \uc2 \f2  (NBH) is the most dovish in the\par region and has kept its benchmark rate at a record low of 0.9%\par since 2016.\par     Hungary's economic growth slowed to an annual\par 4.5% in the fourth quarter from 5.0% in the third quarter,\par matching analyst forecasts and hitting its slowest in almost two\par years, preliminary unadjusted data showed on Friday.\par \par     Hungary's government expects economic growth at 3.5% this\par year, below its previous 4% forecast, Finance Minister Mihaly\par Varga said on Friday. \par     He added that recent falls in the forint were broadly\par neutral for the government budget and reiterated his view that\par Hungary needed a stable and predictable exchange rate.\par \par     "Despite the global and European slowdown the Hungarian\par economy is still growing, and that strengthens the forint," a\par dealer in Budapest said.\par     The Czech crown gained a third of a percent to its\par strongest since October 2012 after inflation grew at its fastest\par pace in almost eight years. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised\par markets with a rate hike last week.\par     The forint's gains also helped the crown's gains as well as\par other regional units, a dealer said. \par     The Czech economy expanded by an annual 1.7% in the fourth\par quarter, below expectations for 1.9% in a Reuters poll, marking\par the slowest pace in six years. \par     The Polish stock market and the zloty\par both traded flat after inflation rose faster than expected in\par January, reaching 4.4% year-on-year, a nine-year high, after a\par 3.4% reading in December.\par     \par   ** For an interactive graphic on GDP: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2qMFUkq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2qMFUkq}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par                     CEE       SNAPSHO   AT                      \par                     MARKETS   T        1049              \par                                        CET               \par                               \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            \par                               IES                        \par                               Latest   Previou  Daily    Change\par                                        s                 \par                               bid      close    change   in 2020\par  EURCZK=  Czech     <EURCZK=  24.7900