\par\par \b \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Yields Little Changed Ahead of Auctions -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2018\par 15:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0935 ET - \uc2 US government\uc2  bonds wobbled around the flatline ahead of a series of Treasury auctions for short-term notes. The yield on the benchmark 10-year \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  note recently traded at 3.062%, compared with 3.065% Monday. Yields, which fall as bond prices rise, slipped overnight as Italian government bonds recovered some of their losses. On tap later Tuesday: auctions for the 4- and 52-week bill, as well as the 2-year note. Signs of weak demand could stoke selling pressure, although some analysts anticipate a relatively quiet trading session ahead of Wednesday's FOMC minutes. (akane.otani@wsj.com; @akaneotani)\par \par \uc2 0806 ET - \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it is likely to keep interest rates steady at 6.5%, a historic low. The message came in minutes to last week's meeting, when the Selic rate was held after 12 consecutive cuts. But it's unclear how markets will react to the communication. Pundits were led to believe the bank would cut last week and many criticized the bank for surprising them. Instability comes from a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which could fuel import prices and inflation. The bank said it is monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact on prices and will react accordingly. (paulo.trevisani@wsj.com; @ptrevisani)\par \par \uc2 0752 ET - Most emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were up against the dollar earlier on Tuesday, including the Turkish lira, but the fall in TRY has resumed again, with USD/TRY up 1% at 4.6234, after reaching a new all-time low of 4.6251. "The vulnerable EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with material idiosyncratic issues continue to underperform," ING says. USD/IDR is also up, albeit by less--0.1% at 14,120. And USD/BRL rises as well, by 0.1% to 3.6778. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0746 ET - The \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only likely to verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the fall of the Hungarian forint, says ING, adding it doesn't "expect no actual NBH response" to the fact that EUR/HUF has risen to 317 from 310 in a month. The three-month Budapest interbank offered rate, or Bubor, has also shot up to 0.1% from 0.02% just a few weeks ago and the 10-year Hungarian forint interest rate swap has risen to 255 basis points on Tuesday, the highest level in a year. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to remain in wait-and-see mode" at the interest rate decision due 1200 GMT, ING says. A lack of NBH response may push EUR/HUF toward the 319 level again, ING adds. EUR/HUF is last down 0.2% at 317.42. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0734 ET - The three-month Budapest interbank offered rate, or Bubor, has shot up to 0.10% from 0.02% a few weeks ago, and the 10-year Hungarian forint interest rate swap has risen to 255 basis points, the highest level in a year, says \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  . This raises questions over whether the \uc2 National Bank of Hungary\uc2  will "double down on its dovish rhetoric and unconventional means to keep both front and long-end yields suppressed," SocGen says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which signaled before that it wants to anchor long-term funding costs and keep the yield curve flat, announces its rate decision at 1200 GMT. EUR/HUF falls 0.2% to 317.36. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0720 ET - The final steps toward a new antiestablishment Italian government presents challenges for the country's economic and sovereign outlook, and may impede progress on the European reform agenda, according to Scope Ratings. The Italian economy holds structural weaknesses tied to its low growth, high public-deficit of 132% of gross domestic product, alongside institutional bottlenecks, and "the composition and inexperience of this probable new government cast doubt on the country's future commitment and ability to resolves such challenges," say analysts Dennis Shen and Giacomo Barisone. The implementation of even some of the suggested measures, probable inaction on other areas of needed reform, and extended political uncertainty cloud the path ahead for Italy's 'A-/Stable' sovereign rating, Scope Ratings' analysts say. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0654 ET - The difficult outlook for gold remains even as falls in the dollar have halted the descent of the metal's price, says spread-betting company IG. "Gold's decline has stalled, which has given precious metal miners a breathing space, but overall the difficult outlook for the commodity remains," says IG's Chris Beauchamp. "It's not clear whether the recent weakness in the dollar marks a top in the rally of the past few months, but with the market still broadly short USD, it's easy to imagine the greenback perking up in due course, even if tomorrow's Fed minutes are not overly hawkish. Ahead of the open, we expect the Dow to start at 25,056, up 43 points from Monday's close." (philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0652 ET - Italian government bonds pare some of Monday's losses but rising five-year credit default swap prices indicate that investors remain concerned over the new government's fiscal plans. "Investors appear concerned over motivations as much as plans," say \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  analysts. While a modification of the fiscal plans may appease President \uc2 Sergio Mattarella\uc2  , "it may require more to ease investor concerns, where a Greek-like crisis is feared, and worse given the size of Italy's economy and market," \uc2 BBH\uc2  analysts say. The 10-year Italian BTP yield is trading 6.2 basis points lower at 2.318% at 1044 GMT, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . The five-year Italian CDS is indicated at 140.85 bps, up from 124.11 bps at the end of last week, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0618 ET - For now, EUR/USD is trading sideways from 1.1750, last up 0.3% at 1.1824 as the spread between 10-year Italian and \uc2 German government\uc2  bonds is narrowing, but if the BTP-Bund spread were to widen to 213 basis points, "then EUR/USD could cascade down to 1.15," according to \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  . "For now though, the rot in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have been stopped." Whether "a tactical bounce follows may boil down to the eurozone flash" PMIs and the Federal Open Market Committee minutes on Wednesday, SocGen says. According to a WSJ poll, manufacturing \uc2 PMI\uc2  likely has stayed flat at 56 and services \uc2 PMI\uc2  likely has fallen to 54.5 in May. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0537 ET - Eight years ago today, on May 22, 2010, the programmer \uc2 Laszlo Hanyecz\uc2  bought two pizzas using 10,000 bitcoin. This is widely recognized as the first real-world transaction using bitcoin. If those pizzas were bought now, with bitcoin trading at $8,268, they would cost $82.7 million--a rather pricey lunch. Commemorating that day puts into perspective how much the cryptocurrency has gained in value since then, and highlights potential issues surrounding its purchasing power in the future. Many critics say, however, that bitcoin could never be a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because its value fluctuates too much. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0511 ET - EUR/USD is likely to stay above the 1.1717 support level on Tuesday, according to ING. With EUR/USD continuing "to be primarily driven by Italian politics and spiking BTP-Bund spreads," EUR/USD is up by 0.1% at 1.1809 as the spread is shrinking, last at 173 basis points. Italian President \uc2 Sergio Mattarella\uc2  is due to meet with the speakers of the lower and upper house today, which \uc2 RBC\uc2  says "many have taken as a sign he will try push back on the League/5 Star plans and their proposed choice for Prime Minister," who is \uc2 Giuseppe Conte\uc2 , a law professor aligned with the Five-Star Movement. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0426 ET - The dollar is reversing early gains versus the euro and now trades lower, with EUR/USD up 0.3% at 1.1827. USD/JPY is still flat at 111.02. Commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also up against the dollar, with USD/CAD down 0.3% at 1.2754 and AUD/USD up 0.3% at 0.7604. "If the strength in risk-related \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  [such as the Australian dollar] proves sustainable, this might pave the way for a reversal in EUR/USD once the BTP-Bund spread starts narrowing again," says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  . EUR/USD has been falling since mid-April, from around 1.24. The spread between 10-year Italian and \uc2 German government\uc2  bonds falls from 185 to 173 basis points Tuesday morning.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 22, 2018 09:35 ET (13:35 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180522ee5m001ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
