\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Crown hits 4-year high, rate hike bets weigh on bonds\b0\par\par\uc2 840 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2017\par 15:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Crown strongest since \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime was launched in\par 2013\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  may improve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rating this week-trader\par \par  (Adds Polish economic figures, weakening of Czech 10-year\par bonds)\par     By Sandor Peto and Jason Hovet\par     BUDAPEST/PRAGUE, Oct 18 (Reuters) - The Czech crown hit a\par four-year high and the zloty tested 3-month highs against the\par euro on Wednesday as Polish retail and industrial data confirmed\par robust economic growth in Central Europe. \par     The crown firmed past 25.7 for the first time\par since the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in late 2013 launched an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par regime to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  week. \par     In April it removed a cap on the crown at 27, letting it\par rise, and in August it started to reverse years of interest rate\par cuts. Another hike may come as early as next month, and that\par prospect, coupled with strong economic figures, lifts the crown.\par  \par     Of the bonds offered by the Czech government at its auction\par on Wednesday, there were no sales of zero-coupon paper. "With\par CNB hikes looming people are not interested in short bonds at\par these levels," a dealer said.\par     After the auction, the Czech 10-year benchmark government\par bond yield, bid at 1.453 percent, reached its highest level\par since August 2014.\par     The crown shrugged off concerns that the likely election\par victory of ANO party at Czech elections over the weekend could\par lead to drawn-out coalition talks, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note.\par \par     "Domestic financial markets are typically resilient to Czech\par political events, given the Czech Republic's strong fiscal\par position, sound institutions and independent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," it\par added. \par     Polish and Czech current account data released this week and\par recent government budget figures have confirmed that most of the\par region's main economies remain well-balanced, analysts said.\par     Polish figures released on Wednesday showed 8.6 percent\par annual surge in retail sales in September, and 4.3 percent rise\par in industrial output.\par     The zloty firmed 0.15 percent to 4.2295 against\par the euro, still a touch off Tuesday's three-month highs.\par     Polish government bonds eased slightly, with the 10-year\par benchmark yield rising 3 basis points to 3.317 percent.\par     The forint, steady on Wednesday at 308.15 per\par euro, reached 5-week highs versus the euro this week. \par     It traded on the firm side of the key psychological line of\par 310, even though \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has flagged further\par monetary easing.\par    "\f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  could lift the outlook of Hungary's debt rating (in\par its review) to positive on Friday, and based on Hungarian\par economic indicators, an upgrade cannot be ruled out either," one\par Budapest-based fixed income trader said.\par     Regional central bankers also watch \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rate setters and any hawkish guidance from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Oct 26\par meeting could reduce appreciation pressure on regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said.\par     \par                CEE MARKETS  SNAPSH   AT  1457 CET         \par                             OT                      \par                             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     \par                             Latest  Previo  Daily   Change\par                                     us              \par                             bid     close   change  in\par                                                     2017\par  Czech crown                25.690  25.784   +0.37   5.13%\par                                  0       5       %  \par  Hungary                    308.15  308.23   +0.03   0.22%\par  forint                         00      00       %  \par  Polish zloty               4.2295  4.2358   +0.15   4.12%\par                                                  %  \par  Romanian leu               4.5875  4.5840  -0.08%  -1.14%\par  Croatian                   7.5080  7.5075  -0.01%   0.63%\par  kuna                                               \par  Serbian                    119.13  119.14   +0.01   3.54%\par  dinar                          00      00       %  \par  Note: daily   calculated   previo  close   1800          \par  change        from         us      at      CET     \par                             STOCKS                        \par                             Latest  Previo  Daily   Change\par                                     us              \par                                     close   change  in\par                                                     2017\par  Prague                     1053.7  1055.9  -0.22%   +14.3\par                                  0       9              3%\par  Budapest                   39075.  38909.   +0.43   +22.1\par                                 18      78       %      0%\par  Warsaw                     2517.8  2514.3   +0.14   +29.2\par                                  2       6       %      6%\par  Bucharest        