\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks march back toward three-year high\b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2017\par 12:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * EM stocks head back toward three-year high\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso gains as metals rally\par \par \uc2 * Philippine's peso rebounds after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to keep rates steady\par \par \uc2 * China sets yuan midpoint rate at 11-month high\par \par \uc2 By Marc Jones\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Aug 22 (Reuters) - Emerging markets, one of 2017's best-performing asset classes, advanced again on Tuesday as stocks climbed back towards three-year highs and a rally in metals markets helped Chile's peso to lead gains by \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MSCI's benchmark emerging stocks index gained 0.5 percent with advances in Hong Kong, China, South Africa and Hungary. It was the index's fourth rise in the past five days, reasserting its outperformance over developed market equities.\par \par \uc2 "At the moment it is the goldilocks scenario," said Cr\u233\'00\'E9dit Agricole emerging market strategist Guillaume Tresca. "Everything seems fine, the latest macro data was quite good, political risk is declining and volatility is okay."\par \par \uc2 Tresca said investors were looking to the annual Jackson Hole conference later this week in the United States, which is hosted by the \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City\uc2 , for insights into global monetary policies.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets have been boosted this year by a weak dollar and by low yields for benchmark U.S and European bonds, which tend to drive global borrowing costs, so this week's signals will be monitored closely.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets continued to feel the effects of a surge in metals prices. Chile, the world's top copper producer, saw its peso strengthen to its highest in more than six months against the dollar, which itself was higher.\par \par \uc2 The geopolitical tension around North Korea eased as the head of the U.S. military's Pacific Command stressed the importance of using diplomacy rather than military force to counter Pyongyang's missile threat.\par \par \uc2 In China, the yuan's official midpoint rate was set at its firmest in 11 months. Mainland Chinese stocks rose again after Shanghai posted its strongest weekly gain in four months last week .\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso, which has fallen to an 11-year low, snapped a 10-day losing streak, as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb speculation.\par \par \uc2 "The BSP will not tolerate ... speculative behaviour and stands ready to use its very ample international reserves and deploy its full policy and regulatory arsenal if necessary," Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas Governor Nestor Espenilla said.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia was expected to keep its key interest rate at 4.75 percent, although the governor of its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hinted at a potential cut "if all indicators support it". Last week, he said the bank was "pretty happy" with the inflation rate, which was 3.88 percent in July.\par \par \uc2 In emerging Europe, \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been in stimulus mode for years, was also expected to leave its base rate unchanged, at a record-low 0.9 percent.\par \par \uc2 The Czech Republic became the first \uc2 European Union\uc2  country to raise rates in five years earlier this month, but Hungary is not expected to move until late next year at the earliest .\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance 2017, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2e7eoml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2e7eoml}}}\uc2  For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance 2017, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2dZbdP5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2dZbdP5}}}\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see) (Reporting by Marc Jones, editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-8-22T11:08:45.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170822ed8m00bm9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
