\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-POLL-Hungarian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seen cutting rates by 15 basis points again\b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2016\par 12:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats Wednesday story to add links to Reuters poll data)\par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/cb-polls?RIC=HUINT%3DECI Reuters Hungary \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate forecasts\par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/econ-polls?RIC=HUCPIAP%3DECI Reuters Hungary average inflation forecasts\par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/econ-polls?RIC=HUGDPAP%3DECI Reuters Hungary GDP forecasts\par \par \uc2 By Sandor Peto\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, April 20 (Reuters) - The \uc2 National Bank of Hungary\uc2  is expected to cut its base rate by 15 basis points at its April 26 meeting and lower it further in the next months, a Reuters poll showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In the April 18-20 poll, 19 out of 21 analysts projected a 15-basis-point reduction to 1.05 percent in the 1.2 percent base rate next week, and two analysts forecast a 10-basis-point cut.\par \par \uc2 Inflation, kept in the negative by a decline in crude and commodities prices, has fuelled expectations for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy easing, mainly in Hungary, but also in Poland.\par \par \uc2 Robust economic growth in the region has buoyed \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Central Europe, also pressing the Czech crown to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cap, and weighing on price levels.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after months of easing through unconventional policy tools, lowered its main interest rate last month, by 15 basis points, resuming the rate cuts which it ended in July last year.\par \par \uc2 It also flagged further easing measures including rate cuts and its deputy governor Marton Nagy said a weaker forint would support exporters and help "desired inflation" return.\par \par \uc2 The forint weakened to 315 against the euro from about 310 after the rate cut, but returned to levels on the firm side of 310 by this week, buoyed by improving economic fundamentals and hopes for upgrades in Hungary's credit ratings.\par \par \uc2 "The exchange rate will absolutely remain a key factor... as long as the forint stays at 310 or firmer, the bank can cut rates further," said Gergely Szabo Forian, portfolio manager of Pioneer Investments.\par \par \uc2 "A change in the international inflation environment, a reversal in the commodities price decline could also bring forward the end of the rate cuts," he added.\par \par \uc2 An interest rate hike by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  in the next months would make \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more cautious, said K&H Bank analyst David Nemeth.\par \par \uc2 "Hungarian and U.S. rates arriving to similar levels would make them thoughtful," he said.\par \par \uc2 According to the median forecasts in the poll, the base rate could bottom out at 0.75 percent in the next months, stay at that level through this year and rise to 0.9 percent by the end of next year.\par \par \uc2 The analysts forecast a pick-up in inflation to 1.6 percent by December this year, 2.4 percent by end-2017 and 2.65 percent by end-2018, still below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 3 percent target. (Editing by Jeremy Gaunt)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-4-25T10:00:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160422ec4m00usd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
