\par\par \b \uc2 Oil Bruises Russian Markets, USD/RUB Nears 80 -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2016\par 17:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1608 GMT A drop in Brent crude futures to levels of around $28 per barrel was in the spotlight on the Russian market Monday. The decline to levels of 2003 poses severe risks for oil-dependent Russia. USD/RUB rallies to 79.43 rubles, heading toward all-time highs of 80.1 seen in December 2014. This sends the dollar-traded RTS index 1.07% lower to 646.01, but helps the ruble-traded Micex to gain 0.85% to 1622.05. \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  loses 1.28%, VTB down 0.14%. \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  falls 0.4%, Lukoil up 0.67%. One should expect Russian markets to reveres only if oil prices rebound, says Renaissance Capital. (andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 1607 GMT Should the Bund futures contract surpass its current record high of 160.69, a one-point jump to 161.7 is set to follow, says Raiffeisen. Meanwhile, a longer-term, five-year technical analysis even supports an advance to unprecedented highs of 172.3 in the coming quarters if the rally proves to have legs, it adds. The Eurex-listed continuous contract is trading at 160.37 Monday, flat for the day but still within touching distance of all-time highs. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1605 GMT The 0.82% yield of Romania's 1-year discounted bill, auctioned earlier today, is well below expectations of circa 0.9% by Piraeus Bank Romania. The issue was also oversubscribed by 2.6 times and came 15 bps below the last 1-year auction in December. However, fiscal risks should not be overlooked, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Erste Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  before the transaction, as 2016 will bring parliamentary elections. In addition, capital flows towards emerging markets could become more selective, but it still sees Romania's macroeconomic outlook as stable for now. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1603 GMT While the bank forecasts no more rate cuts, unconventional easing measures are likely. Furthermore, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  retains a bias for a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support growth, in line with the government's objective and to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  profitable as a weak HUF increases the HUF-value of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves. Hungary's growth is set to decelerate in 2016, primarily on the back of a decrease in public investment driven by reduced \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  support funds inflows. DB looks to capture this via going long PLN/HUF, with a target at 75 and stop at 70.4. PLN/HUF is at 70.77. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1602 GMT The bank says it regards long-maturity local-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Hungarian bonds "as one of our favorite positions" and sees room for 10-year maturity local-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bond yields to rally to 2.90%, from 3.31% at present. Hungary has a clear ascension path to investment grade in 2016 and a relative insensitivity to external risks including China's slowdown, falling commodities prices and rising U.S. interest rates. Hungarian foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bond yield differentials' "recent performance--with only moderate widening amidst global risk aversion--attests to this." Favors EUR-denominated Hungarian bonds maturing in 2019 over USD-denominated bonds. Recommends switching from Romanian bonds maturing in 2024 to Hungarian bonds maturing in 2024. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1602 GMT Chances of further action from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have increased, according to Pictet, but so has the prospect that it will further stress its focus on underlying measures of inflation and not the headline figure. This will happen to prevent an overreaction to an inflation outlook that is weak almost exclusively due to lower oil, says economist Frederik Ducrozet. He expects \f28 \uc2 \f2 the ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  to pull the trigger in March at the earlier but more likely in June, using deposit rate cuts to address tightening financial conditions and quantitative easing for low inflation. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1549 GMT The ruble weakens 2.2% to 79.31 a dollar, heading toward all-time highs above 80 rubles, a level last seen in December 2014. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprombank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says the ruble's main driver is the price of Brent crude, which is likely to rebound to $30 per barrel this week. The state-owned bank recommends in a note to clients to buy Brent, while selling USD/RUB. It's target fo rthe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair is 75 rubles. (andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1541 GMT The Federation of German Industries says the country's exports to Iran could double within five years from EUR2.4 billion currently following the lifting of sanctions. A modernization of the oil industry gives German machinery and plant makers large business opportunities, according to the group. There are further opportunities in automotive manufacturing, the chemical industry, healthcare, renewable energy, waste management and construction materials, it notes. (friedrich.geiger@wsj.com, @FGeiger_WSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1525 GMT Central European countries -- as oil importers -- would benefit from low oil prices, says Erste Bank. If oil prices stay close to $30/bbl for 2016, the region's GDP growth could be 0.2pp higher than otherwise, it adds. The region would benefit from rising household income as well as from higher demand from other non-producers, it says. Inflation would be about 0.2pp-0.3pp lower than expected, and monetary policy would remain accommodative for longer. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  would likely maintain its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy for at least another quarter and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could surprise with another 30-40bp in rate cuts. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1430 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faces one of its most difficult decisions in years this week. On Wednesday, it will decide whether to raise the 14.25% Selic benchmark rate amid a deep recession, to fight double-digit inflation. Even analysts are split, with some recommending an increase to convince markets that it's serious about bringing inflation back within its target range this year; and others saying that such a move would worsen the recession. The latter group argues that monetary tightening takes longer to show results in Brazil because of heavy indexation, so the bank'd better wait. The bank also faces political pressure to hold ahead of municipal elections. (paulo.trevisani@wsj.com; @ptrevisani) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1235 GMT Protection on European corporate and financial bonds is rapidly becoming more expensive, as reflected on iTraxx indexes, showing that the sector is under "severe stress", says \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The iTraxx Crossover index of sub-investment grade entity credit default swaps is approaching its highest level since late 2014, while the iTraxx Europe is already at its highest since the second half of 2013. The corporate and financial bond segments, which offer a pick-up over safer fixed income assets, have been in vogue with many investors over the past two years, adds RBC. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1224 GMT When the ruble was hitting record lows in late 2014, Russian companies and households were contributing to the rapid depreciation as they ditched rubles for hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Now, as oil prices are sending the ruble back toward those record lows, there's less of a rush to stock up with dollars. "We note no elevated demand for hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the local side, with the ruble continuing to move in line with external factors," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 VTB Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2 . USD/RUB is 1.3% higher at 78.64 rubles. (andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 18, 2