\par\par \b \uc2 CEE Morning Briefing: Hungary Seen Holding Rates\b0\par\par\uc2 By Margit Feher   \par \uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2015\par 05:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 0900/0800 Hungarian public debt \par           at end-September \par 1400/1300 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central \par           bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate decision \par 1500/1400 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par           publishes statement \par           on rate decision \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungary is widely expected to keep its main policy rate at its current record low on Tuesday, as its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has pledged to keep monetary conditions loose with measures other than interest-rate cuts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Bank of Hungary\uc2  is exploring unconventional easing steps as they may prove more effective in targeting certain parts of the economy than an across-the-board rate cuts, Deputy Governor Marton Nagy said earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to maintain its current record low 1.35% benchmark interest rate, possibly into 2019, Mr. Nagy has said.\par \par \uc2 "The monetary policy council has signaled more unconventional measures [to come] to support growth, most likely relating to more incentives for banks to increase lending," \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  said in a note to clients. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par 0350 GMT  27.013-73 \par Previous  27.012-74 \par %Chg 0.00 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par 0350 GMT 311.71-2.23 \par Previous 311.55-2.07 \par %Chg  +0.05 \par  \par EUR/P