\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2-Hungary's bonds snapped up at auction, Serbian cbank buys euros\b0\par\par\uc2 791 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2015\par 14:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds Serbian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bond auctions, new slug)\par     By Krisztina  Than\par     BUDAPEST, Oct 15 (Reuters) - Hungarian government bond\par auctions attracted good demand on Thursday especially from local\par banks keen to invest extra funds freed up by several \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures.\par     The forint traded 0.2 percent firmer after the\par auctions while the region's other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were broadly flat.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Serbia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought euros on the domestic interbank\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to stem gains by the dinar, dealers said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which on Wednesday cut its benchmark\par interest rate to 4.50 percent, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the dinar\par  trading at 119.70 to the euro, 0.25 percent stronger\par than a day earlier. After the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , at 1132 GMT the\par dinar was trading more weakly at 119.90.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made a series of changes in\par recent months to squeeze liquidity out of its own instruments\par and encourage banks to buy government debt instead. In its\par latest move, it lowered the reserve ratio for commercial banks,\par launching a uniform 2 percent ratio. These measures have boosted\par local banks' appetite for government securities.\par     "There has been significant local demand for government\par papers," a fixed income trader said. "This (in past weeks) has\par been pushing down yields from 3-month treasury bills up to 3-5\par year bonds."\par     The trader said the impact from increased local demand was\par less palpable on 10-year gove rnment bonds.\par     Hungary sold 56 billion forints worth of bonds at an auction\par on Thursday, more than the offer of 47 billion forints\par . It sold more of the 3-year and 5-year bonds than\par planned. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held \f28 \uc2 \f2 IRS\f28 \uc2 \f2  (interest rate swap) tenders\par  on Thursday, which are intended to be a hedging\par instrument, supporting banks in increasing and stabilising their\par holdings of long-term government securities.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  accepted 48.3 billion forints worth of\par bids, versus its offer of 65 billion.\par     In Poland, debt yields fell on Wednesday, tracking core\par markets, and eased further on Thursday. \par     Disappointing economic data from the United States resulted\par in yield drops abroad and Polish bonds followed suit.\par     The Polish debt market is expected to remain under the\par influence of core markets, where expectations for an early rate\par rise by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  have been weakening, PKO \f28 \uc2 \f2 BP\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts\par wrote in a note.\par     Polish bonds may also be impacted by a final September CPI\par reading for Poland, which was to be published at 1200 GMT.\par     Stock markets were in positive territory, with Warsaw\par  leading gains, rising 0.7 percent by 1132 GMT.  \par  *                                                            *\par  **************** 