\par\par \b \uc2 Hungary Rate Cut Now Off The Table, RBS Says -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2015\par 11:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0931 GMT Further Hungarian interest rate cuts are now off the table given increased risks related to Greece, says RBS. RBS had called previously for a 1.2%-1.3% bottom in the policy rate compared to 1.5% currently. Should Greece pressures intensify, \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely use verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  but won't raise rates this year, says economist Gabor Ambrus. Hungary's record low policy rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity measures to keep short-end cash rates low for an extended period "have created added vulnerabilities for the forint. This matters more than the cushion provided by the strong current account surplus." RBS retains its short HUF call and thinks EUR/HUF could trade above 320 in the coming months. EUR/HUF is at 317.21. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 08, 2015 05:31 ET (09:31 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150708eb7800117\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
