\par\par \b \uc2 Hungary, Factors to watch, Jan 19\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2015\par 08:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, Jan 19 (Reuters) - Following is a list of events in Hungary and the region, as well as news stories and press reports which may influence financial markets.               \par \par \uc2 (For any queries: Budapest editorial +36 1 327 4745)                              \par \par \uc2 WHAT IS HAPPENING IN HUNGARY (ALL TIMES GMT)               \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST - No events of note.                              \par \par \uc2 IN THE REGION               \par \par \uc2 ROMANIA - T-bond tender               \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA - T-bond tender (0900)               \par \par \uc2 CZECH - Feb T-bill calendar (1300)                              \par \par \uc2 IN THE NEWS REUTERS               \par \par \uc2 HUNGARY'S ORBAN RULES OUT STATE HELP WITH SWISS FRANC LOANS               \par \par \uc2 Hungary's banks and borrowers will have to negotiate over the spiralling cost of Swiss-franc consumer loans without further state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Prime Minister \uc2 Viktor Orban\uc2  said on Sunday.                              \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HUNGARY CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO LOOK PAST 2015 INFLATION RISKS               \par \par \uc2 Downside risks to Hungary's 2015 inflation have increased but recent price falls have not spilled over into future expectations and the outlook for 2016 has not changed, the \uc2 National Bank of Hungary\uc2  told Reuters on Friday.                              \par \par \uc2 C.EUROPEAN ASSETS REBOUND AND RATE CUT EXPECTATIONS SURVIVE PLUNGE               \par \par \uc2 Polish and Hungarian assets appeared to be stabilizing on Friday as analysts said the negative economic impacts of Thursday's surge of the Swiss franc could be smaller than initially feared.                              \par \par \uc2 HUNGARY PICKS ECONOMIST BARCZA AS DEBT AGENCY CHIEF               \par \par \uc2 Hungary's economy minister has named Gyorgy Barcza as the new head of the government debt agency AKK, the ministry said in a statement on Friday.                              \par \par \uc2 HUNGARY'S NOV CONSTRUCTION OUTPUT GROWTH SLOWS TO 8.8 PCT Y/Y               \par \par \uc2 Hungary's construction sector output expanded by an annual 8.8 percent in November following a 15.8 percent rise in October, the Central Statistics Office (KSH) said on Friday.                              \par \par \uc2 KBC'S HUNGARIAN UNIT SAYS ITS SWISS FRANC EXPOSURE IS COVERED               \par \par \uc2 KBC Bank's Hungarian unit said on Friday that it had already closed its CHF/EUR position linked to the conversion of its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mortgage stock and only had a limited exposure.                              \par \par \uc2 AUSTRIAN BANKS COUNT COST OF EASTERN TROUBLES               \par \par \uc2 Austrian banks' longstanding ties with central and eastern European neighbours provided years of profits when they moved in quickly after the fall of the Soviet Union. But Ukraine's descent into chaos, Russia's economic crisis, political turmoil in Hungary and sluggish Romanian growth caught them out and led to a series of profit warnings, exposing risk management failings and a culture of hoping for the best.                              \par \par \uc2 INTERVIEW-SLOVENIA EXPECTS SALE OF TELECOM FIRM, NO 2 BANK IN FEBRUARY               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-19T08:11:36.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150119eb1j00645\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
