\par\par \b \uc2 *Hungary Matolcsy: Portfolio Cleaning First Step in MKB Reorganization\b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2014\par 09:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 18 Dec 2014 03:17 ET *Hungary Matolcsy: Recommends Privatization of MKB After Reorganization\par \par \uc2 18 Dec 2014 03:20 ET *Hungary PM: Commercial Banks Shouldn't Be in Permanent State Ownership\par \par \uc2 18 Dec 2014 03:27 ET *Hungary PM: Forint Vulnerability a Concern Due to Still High Public Debt\par \par \uc2 18 Dec 2014 03:28 ET *Hungary Export Hit By Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Crisis, EU Sanctions-PM\par \par \uc2 18 Dec 2014 03:31 ET *Hungary Matolcsy: No Forint Story, HUF Reflects Ruble Movements Now\par \par \uc2 18 Dec 2014 03:31 ET *Hungary Matolcsy: \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Only Anchor is Medium-Term CPI Target\par \par \uc2 18 Dec 2014 03:32 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  Matolcsy: No Obligation, Pressure to \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Market Developments\par \par \uc2 18 Dec 2014 03:33 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  Financial System Stable, Well-Protected -Matolcsy\par \par \uc2 18 Dec 2014 04:06 ET  Hungary Hit by Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Crisis But Economy Stable -Matolcsy\par \par \uc2 By Veronika Gulyas and Margit Feher\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST--The \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under no obligation or pressure to defend the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Thursday after the forint weakened to multi-year record lows against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to contagion from the Russia's ruble crisis.\par \par \uc2 "There's no forint story, just a ruble story," National Bank of Hungary governor Gyorgy Matolcsy said at a press conference.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian forint weakened Wednesday to a three-year low against the euro and a 12-year low against the dollar on the Russian ruble's woes.\par \par \uc2 Despite this the economy is stable and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements are solely due to the ruble movements, Mr. Matolcsy said.\par \par \uc2 The governor confirmed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate goal, its only anchor is the medium-term inflation target.\par \par \uc2 "There's neither obligation nor pressure to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in market developments," Mr. Matolcsy added.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian economy is affected negatively by the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis since the forint is vulnerable due to Hungary's high public debt and its households' foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt, Hungarian Prime Minister \uc2 Viktor Orban\uc2  said at the same briefing.\par \par \uc2 Hungary had also planned to increase its exports to Russia but the extreme ruble weakening against core \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's sanctions against Russia over Ukraine hit Hungary's plans, Mr. Orban added.\par \par \uc2 Write to Veronika Gulyas at veronika.gulyas@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @VeronikaGulyas1 and Margit Feher at margit.feher@wsj.com \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @margitfeher\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 18, 2014 04:06 ET (09:06 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141218eaci001ej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
