\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Loose monetary policy may limit CEE  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  gains\b0\par\par\uc2 868 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2014\par 12:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Zloty seen flat in coming weeks, gradually firmer next year\par \par \uc2 * Gains smaller, risks are loose monetary policy, Ukraine, \uc2 Fed\par \par \uc2 * Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan conversion could cause forint jitters\par \par \uc2 By Sandor Peto\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, Sept 4 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty may gain more than 3 percent against the euro over the next 12 months as \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Central Europe firm up, a Reuters poll of analysts showed.\par \par \uc2 The region's biggest economies have grown faster than those of euro zone states while inflation across the region is low or even in negative territory in Poland's case.\par \par \uc2 Their recovery from the previous decade's global economic crisis is slowing and central banks in the region find themselves being nudged towards looser monetary policy, also partly due to the Ukrainian crisis.\par \par \uc2 That risk is reflected in the forecasts in the poll, which show weaker exchange rates for the zloty and the forint than the median forecasts in a survey conducted a month ago.\par \par \uc2 The Sept 2-3 poll of 21 analysts showed that the zloty is expected to move sideways near 4.2 to the euro in the coming weeks and firm up to 4.074 by September next year, compared with 4.03 projected in the previous poll.\par \par \uc2 The forint is expected to firm up by 1.7 percent from Wednesday's close to 309 by next September, a slightly softer forecast than last month's 305. The Czech crown could gain 2 percent to 27.15, and the leu 0.3 percent to 4.39.\par \par \uc2 Tit-for-tat sanctions between the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and Russia have clouded the economic outlook for Central European states and caused some jitters in their markets in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks jumped on Wednesday after Ukrainian and Russian leaders said they were moving closer to a political solution to the battle between Kiev's forces and Moscow-backed rebels in eastern Ukraine. But doubts remain.\par \par \uc2 "The conflict over Ukraine may not yet be over, so short-term risks (to the zloty) remain," said Piotr Poplawski, analyst at BGZ Bank in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveiled a four-year funding plan called TLTROs for banks in June and may flag more monetary stimulus on Thursday, which could also fuel appetite for the assets of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 "The ECB's TLTRO \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  should help the zloty gain," said Poplawski.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its own 2.5 percent main interest rate on hold on Wednesday but Governor Marek Belka said rate cuts were likely if economic figures in the coming weeks continue to indicate weakness.\par \par \uc2 Belka said that economic weakness in the euro zone had a much bigger impact on Poland than the Ukrainian crisis and that the exchange rate was not an important factor in rate decisions.\par \par \uc2 Top Polish economic policy makers have said several times, though, that a firming of the zloty would be more worrying for the economy than a depreciation.\par \par \uc2 "We believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has little tolerance for a strengthening of the PLN (zloty)," said \uc2 Nordea\uc2  analyst Anders Svendsen in a note. "A move towards 4.10 could be enough to prompt a rate cut given the circumstances."\par \par \uc2 FORINT VULNERABLE\par \par \uc2 The zloty, as the region's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is particularly exposed to any downturn in international market sentiment if the Ukraine crisis deepens or expectations for an early start to \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  rate hikes strengthen.\par \par \uc2 The forint is also vulnerable as junk-rated Hungary has the highest debt in the region at more than 80 percent of economic output. In addition, its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has steadily cut its main interest rate to 2.1 percent, below investment grade Poland's main rate.\par \par \uc2 The median forecasts in the poll show a slight weakening of the forint to 315 by October, a 1 percent gain to 311-311.50 on the 3- and 6-month horizons and further gains thereafter.\par \par \uc2 Several analysts warned, however, that those forecasts for given points in the calendar hide likely forint jitters.\par \par \uc2 "I expect a weakening in January that could push the forint to about 320 against the euro due to the planned conversion of banks' foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans (worth around $15 billion)," said Andras Balatoni, analyst at \uc2 ING Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some analysts expect the first wave of forint weakening to come late this month or in October if the government announces the details of the conversions.\par \par \uc2 However, the government will do its best later this year to strengthen the forint by policy measures or by trying to talk it up, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may even \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Part of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's debt is in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and only stronger forint levels could reduce the level of state debt below 80 percent of output by the end of the year, averting the threat of financial sanctions from the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "By my calculations only forint levels at 307 would result in a decline in debt (from end-2013 levels)," said Gergely Gabler, analyst of \uc2 Erste Group\uc2  in Budapest.\par \par \uc2 For data please click on\par \par \uc2 Latest Reuters polls on major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 : (Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-7T10:50:12.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140904ea94009c5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
