\par\par \b \uc2 *\uc2 Hungary  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Has No Foreign  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Rate Target-Gerhardt\b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2014\par 16:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2014 10:38 EDT *\uc2 Hungary \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Gerhardt Reacts to HUF Weakness\par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2014 10:39 EDT *Hungary Central Banker Gerhardt Made Comment to Portfolio.hu\par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2014 10:41 EDT *Hungary Gerhardt: Hasn't Made In-Depth Calculations on Impact of Current HUF Levels\par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2014 11:00 EDT  \uc2 Hungary \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Has No Exchange Rate Target-Gerhardt\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Veronika Gulyas \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUDAPEST--The \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Hungary\f28 \uc2 \f2  has no exchange rate target, Ferenc Gerhardt, one of the two deputy governors of the bank told business website Portfolio.hu on Thursday, in a reaction to the forints easing against the euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Processes are relatively new, there's too little information; we haven't made in-depth calculations based on the actual facts yet," Mr. Gerhardt said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He also noted he cannot add much to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Gyorgy Matolcsy's comments on Wednesday when he said there was ample room for further rate cuts in Hungary.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The forint weakened to a two-year low versus the euro earlier on Thursday. The euro-forint traded at HUF309.71 at 1547 GMT versus 312.42 at around 1000 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts at BudaCash said market participants expect Mr. Matolcsy to verbally \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and halt the forint from further weakening; and also to prove its independence from the government.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors have drawn a parallel with Turkey, suspecting that due to the political considerations of the government, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be just as unwilling as its Turkish counterpart to increase rates, BudaCash analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro-forint rate may rise further even to the HUF320 level until the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  verbally \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a local trader who preferred to remain anonymous said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Veronika Gulyas at veronika.gulyas@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 30, 2014 11:00 ET (16:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140130ea1u002nd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
