\par\par \b \uc2 Long EUR/HUF Favored On CB Inaction: SocGen -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2014\par 13:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1238 GMT [Dow Jones] After rate hikes from Turkey and South Africa, focus in the EMEA region has now turned to Hungary. SocGen says both the CBRT and SARB acted to protect financial stability, defend against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pass-through to inflation, and stem \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation. However, the bank does not expect the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to follow suit, neither reversing its 18-month easing cycle before the April general elections or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend any run on the HUF. The bank favors a long EUR/HUF trade to play out this scenario, targeting 329.26 on a 3-month horizon with a protective stop down at 301.31. EUR/HUF now 311.60. gary.stride@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 7:30 EST - Gains for US stock-index futures have been building as the morning progresses after the market's latest slide Wednesday. Moving further into the green is a good sign considering the recent trend of futures fading as the opening bell nears and then getting worse from there. There's plenty to chew on besides EM and the FOMC, between the rush of quarterly reports this morning and economic data which includes jobless claims and the first read on 4Q GDP--which should look strong amid increasing inventories and a still-falling trade gap. S&P 500 futures are up 5.5 as gold drops and oil is modestly higher. The euro is solidly lower, breaching $1.36, and Treasurys are giving back a bit of yesterday's gains. The 10-year yield is at 2.70%. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1144 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/ZAR eases back from a fresh 5-year high of 11.3915 to 11.24, and USD/TRY slips to 2.2620 from the day's 2.3013 peak. These moves remove the immediate need for JPY as a safe haven play and USD/JPY recovers to 102.46 from a session low of 102.12, while EUR/JPY climbs from a fresh 8-week low of 138.90 to 139.50. gary.stride@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 1131 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: Indonesia likely continued to post a trade surplus in December, as a falling rupiah and slowing economic activity curbed imports. The country may have recorded a trade surplus of $729.5 million in December, according to a median poll of 10 regional economists. That could mean a surplus for a third consecutive month following surpluses of $776.8 million in November and $42.4 million in October. Other surpluses beyond the fourth quarter were recorded in August and March. "We are also starting to see signs that the worst may be over for export growth. On sequential terms, both the total volume and value of exports have been gaining ground since the third quarter," says DBS economist Gundy Cahyadi. Indonesia's December trade data is due Monday around 0430 GMT. (andreasismar.sandiwan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1117 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/DKK has been trading well above its central rate of 7.46038 for over two weeks, reaching a 5-year high of 7.4651 on Monday. At these levels, \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  says there is legitimate risk that \uc2 Danmarks Nationalbank\uc2  will eventually need to support DKK with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a 10 basis point rate hike. EUR/DKK now at 7.4622 gary.stride@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 1114 GMT [Dow Jones] The ruble was widely expected to firm at the beginning of 2014 thanks to favorable seasonal factors and the Sochi Winter Olympics, while the Bank of Russia was seen cutting interest rates slightly in the second half of this year when inflation slows to target. Instead, the ruble has fallen to all-time lows versus the euro and the basket, which is likely to boost inflation as imported goods will become more expensive. Uralsib Capital expects the weaker ruble to fuel inflation by 0.5% (so far) this year, which could prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from monetary easing this year. (andrey.ostroukh@dowjones.com) Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 1058 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  says evidence from German states that have already reported January CPI data Thursday point to the preliminary National CPI falling by 0.6% on the month and to +1.3% on the year, against forecasts of -0.5% and +1.5% respectively. Data is out 1300 GMT. gary.stride@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 1057 GMT xxxx GMT Financial markets want the \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prove its independence, says brokerage BudaCash. Investors have drawn a parallel with Turkey, suspecting that due to political considerations of the government, \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be just as unwilling as its Turkish counterpart to increase rates, BudaCash analysts say. \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  communication is becoming vital since the HUF has weakened to a two-year record against the EUR, they add. \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head Gyorgy Matolcsy "should become more practical" and shouldn't stick to inflation as the sole factor driving the bank's policy rate, they add. Markets await Mr. Matolcsy, previously the country's economy minister before taking the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helm, to verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the analysts note. (margit.feher@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1049 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: Indonesia's inflation is likely to remain elevated in January on high food prices as floods hamper distribution. On-year, inflation may hit 8.30% in January, according to a Dow Jones poll of nine regional economists, easing slightly from December's 8.38%. On-month, the consumer price index likely rose 1.0% in January versus a 0.55% increase in December, according to seven of the economists. Bank Indonesia Senior Deputy Gov. Mirza Adityaswara on Jan. 24 tipped January's on-month inflation to come in between 0.85% and 1%. "We expect inflation to stay on its seasonal path, with the heavy rainy season in January causing floods and traffic jams in many regions and thus disturbing food distribution," says Bank Danamon economist Anton Gunawan. (andreasismar.sandiwan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1040 GMT xxxx GMT Hungary has no room to cut rates further in light of the current steep weakening of the HUF and despite comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head that rates could go even lower, brokerage BudaCash says. Following a string of 18 consecutive monthly rate cuts, the \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "cannot strain" investor nerves further, economist Toth Gergely says. The main rate has reached the bottom at its current all-time low of 2.85%, he adds. HUF weakened to a new two-year record against the euro Thursday morning. The bond market is already pricing in rate hikes for the next six months, he notes. Hungary "could reverse the course of its monetary easing with cautious rate increases in the coming months," he adds. (margit.feher@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1023 GMT [Dow Jones] Although it doesn't see a March \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  rate cut, \uc2 SEB Bank\uc2  says Norway's unclear growth outlook and ongoing macroeconomic uncertainty will dissuade foreign investors from returning to Norwegian asset markets near-term, and weigh on NOK. The bank sees limited 2014 upside in EUR/NOK, probably to the 8.50-8.60 zone (8.48 now), but favors long USD/NOK from the current 6.16 level for a move to 6.50, with a stop down at 6.05. gary.stride@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 1015 GMT [Dow Jones] The euro-forint rate may rise further - even to 320 - until the \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a local trader says. EUR/HUF is at 311.19 after testing a two-year high 312 earlier Thursday. The trader notes that there are many stop-loss positions around this level and trading currently points further upward. The 320 level is EUR/HUF's all-time high, hit in late 2011. (veronika.gulyas@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 30, 2014 07:38 ET (12:38 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140130ea1u001n3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
