\par\par \b \uc2 CEE Morning Briefing: Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Likely Leave Rates Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 By Leos Rousek   \par \uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2014\par 04:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par     N/A    \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate decision \par  0830/0730 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Dec \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Fx\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves \par  0900/0800 Hungary Nov industrial output \par  1400/1300 Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Dec minutes \par  1600/1500 Hungary govt prelim 2013 budget balance \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Narodowy Bank Polski\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is likely to leave its reference interest rate unchanged at a record low of 2.5%, reflecting tame inflationary pressures amid the local economy's gradual recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 NBP lowered its base interest rate to the current level in July when it ended a series of monetary policy easings launched in November 2012.\par \par \uc2 The country's annual inflation slowed to 0.6% in November from 0.8% in October, well below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2.5% target.\par \par \uc2 Investors expect the bank to confirm its earlier stated goal to leave borrowing costs unchanged through mid-2014 and wait for the economy to accelerate its growth.\par \par \uc2 In Budapest, investors will focus on November industrial output and end-December budget balance readings.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the country's industrial output to have accelerated to 7% on the year in November, from 6% a month earlier. Earlier this month some government officials said the 2013 fiscal budget deficit was likely to have stayed below the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's threshold set at 3% of gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Latest 0250 GMT 27.455-98 \par Previous 2150 GMT 27.459-504 \par %Chg -0.02 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0250 GMT 299.94-300.56 \par Previous 2150 GMT 299.66-300.50 \par % Chg   +0.06 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0250 GMT  4.1745-96 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.1726-99 \par % Chg  +0.02 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par         Tue    Mon \par 3 yrs   3.94%  3.98% \par 5 yrs   4.62%  4.65% \par 10yrs   5.58%  5.59% \par Poland \par          Tue    Mon \par 3 yrs    3.03%  3.03% \par 5 yrs    3.72%  3.72% \par 10yrs    4.45%  4.46% \par  \par  \par Czech Republic \par          Tue    Mon \par 3 yrs    0.59%  0.59% \par 5 yrs    1.26%  1.24% \par 10yrs    2.50%  2.51% \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par 2,349.60-55.62-2.31% \par  \par BUX \par 18,618.66+45.89+0.25% \par  \par PX \par 988.15-1.44-0.15% \par  \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's prime minister Tuesday waded into a high-pitched British row over welfare benefits for migrant workers, insisting his \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  state would veto any proposed changes at the European level.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Centre-right Prime Minister Donald Tusk made the statement after his British counterpart David Cameron urged changes to EU treaties allowing the U.K. to withhold welfare benefits like child allowances for workers from other member states.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The head of the Czech Automotive Industry Association believes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts to weaken the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will fail to lift foreign sales of domestic-made automobiles, one part of the broader goal of the last year's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HUNGARY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's partly state-owned Szechenyi Bank Zrt. is likely to buy the local arm of Austrian lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Raiffeisen Bank International AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RBI.VI), including all its losses and receivables, for a symbolic 1 euro ($1.4), Hungarian online business news agency napi.hu says Tuesday, without naming its sources.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Monday, an unconfirmed report was published by Hungarian daily Magyar Hirlap saying the minor Hungarian lender made the buyout offer for Raiffeisen's local unit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Leos Rousek at leos.rousek@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new WSJ and Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 07, 2014 22:11 ET (03:11 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140108ea18000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
