\par\par \b \uc2 CEE Morning Briefing: EC Issues View on Slovenian Bank Support\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney  \par \uc2 863 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2013\par 04:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 1400/1300 Polish November industrial output \par N/A EU Commission issues report on Slovenian banking sector support \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Slovenia's troubled state-owned lenders will be closely watched Wednesday if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the executive branch of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , releases its verdict on whether a planned capital injection in the banks is in line with the bloc's anti-trust regulations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Last week the Slovenian government said it would be able to finance the recapitalization without an international bailout despite a capital shortfall of 3.01 billion euros ($4.15 billion) at the three largest state-owned banks.\par \par \uc2 The capital shortfall was revealed by bank stress tests that also asked five other smaller Slovenian banks, which aren't controlled by the state, to raise an extra EUR1.77 billion so they could survive another major downturn in the country's economy. However those banks will be given six months to raise the money on the market or secure it from their foreign owners.\par \par \uc2 Separately, Poland is expected to report a 1.2% annual increase in industrial output for November.\par \par \uc2 A marked improvement of the manufacturing Purchasing Manager Index for Poland over the past few months shows the economy is gaining steam again and that it has emerged from stagnation earlier this year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0250 GMT 27.679-718 \par Previous 2150 GMT 27.664-705 \par %Chg +0.05 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0250 GMT 298.69-9.04 \par Previous 2150 GMT 298.45-9.13 \par % Chg  +0.02 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0250 GMT 4.1767-836 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.1770-835 \par % Chg   0.00 \par  \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par          Tues   Mon \par 3 yrs    4.05%  4.08% \par 5 yrs    4.67%  4.70% \par 10yrs    5.65%  5.68% \par  \par Poland \par          Tues   Mon \par 3 yrs    2.99%  2.98%(1) \par 5 yrs    3.56%  3.55% \par 10yrs    4.40%  4.37% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par          Tues   Mon \par 3 yrs    0.24%  0.24% \par 5 yrs    0.79%  0.77% \par 10yrs    2.27%  2.24%(1) \par (1) 11 yrs \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par 2,392.26-41.21-1.69% \par  \par BUX \par 18,617.52-163.49-0.87% \par  \par PX \par 962.28-3.98-0.41% \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  aims to limit the strength of the koruna until early 2015, Governor Miroslav Singer said Tuesday after the bank reaffirmed its goal of using \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as its key policy tool.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Last month, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ordered its traders to buy the euro with the aim of bringing the exchange rate close to 27 against the European common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened the koruna by about 5% within a day.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HUNGARY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Hungary on Tuesday continued its rollback of privatization in the energy sector and moved a step closer toward creating a state-owned telecommunications operator, part of a push for an expanded government role in the nation's economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ruling Fidesz party has said the state should buy stakes in companies it regards as strategically important, including utilities. The government has said the sale of such businesses to private investors in the 1990s, when Hungary was moving to a market economy and leaving behind central planning after the fall of the Iron Curtain, was a mistake.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary's state-owned utility MVM Zrt. said Tuesday that it will buy a minority stake in Fogaz Zrt., which supplies natural gas to 820,000 households and business customers in Budapest, from German utility firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 RWE AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (RWE.XE).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MVM will pay 41 billion forints ($187.4 million) for RWE International B.V.'s 49.8% stake in Fogaz, it said. MVM will finance the purchase from funds it will receive through the national asset management company \f28 \uc2 \f2 MNV Zrt\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UKRAINE: Russia trumped the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  by extending a bailout package worth as much as $20 billion to neighboring Ukraine, showing the importance Moscow places on keeping the former Soviet republic in its orbit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pact, one of the richest ever offered by Russia to another country, came just weeks after Kiev turned its back on a trade deal with the EU that Moscow had strongly opposed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The deal, announced after talks in the Kremlin between Russian President Vladimir Putin and his Ukrainian counterpart Viktor Yanukovych on Tuesday, gives Ukraine loans and cheaper natural-gas supplies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BULGARIA: Bulgaria's foreign minister said Tuesday he had postponed a December trip to Britain because of a row triggered by London's fears of an influx of Bulgarians and Romanians next year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We felt the atmosphere was not suitable," Kristian Vigenin was quoted by Bulgarian media as saying on the sidelines of a Brussels meeting of \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  foreign ministers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Marcin Sobczyk in Warsaw and Leos Rousek in Prague contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/ }}}\uc2 \f2  for the WSJ blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 17, 2013 22:06 ET (03:06 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131218e9ci000eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
