\par\par \b \uc2 Hungarian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  chief raises prospect of rate cuts\b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2013\par 15:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Inflation fell in October close to 40-year low\par \par \uc2 * Matolcsy rules out Czech-style \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Says stimulus fund could help meet inflation target\par \par \uc2 By Leigh Thomas\par \par \uc2 PARIS, Nov 12 (Reuters) - Hungary could cut interest rates to counter falling inflation, its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor told Reuters on Tuesday, ruling out Czech-style \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hungarian inflation dropped close to a 40-year low of 0.9 percent last month, well below economists' average forecast of 1.4 percent, official data showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Inflation is falling across the region and the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week for the first time in more than a decade to counter the risk of a debt-deflation spiral.\par \par \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Gyorgy Matolcsy said in an interview that while falling inflation presented a policy "challenge", \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not the right option for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the economy was too small and debt levels - especially in the hands of foreigners - were high.\par \par \uc2 "We have to be very cautious," he said on the sidelines of a conference in Paris. "We don't have a policy to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that means very, very small steps can be used."\par \par \uc2 He said such steps could include interest rate cuts, though he added this would be up to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee to decide.\par \par \uc2 Matolcsy, a former economy minister, added that another option was to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $12.5 billion stimulus plan.\par \par \uc2 "It might help to reach the inflation target" of 3 percent, he said.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian forint fell to six-week lows on Tuesday after the low inflation figure, which Matolcsy said was partly due to one-off influences such as a 20 percent reduction in energy prices.\par \par \uc2 "But there are longer-term trends (at play), meaning weak consumption, higher savings and very strong motivation on the part of Hungarian households to lower their debt levels," he said. (Reporting by Leigh Thomas; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY-CBANK/ | ABN | M | E | RBN | D | HX | BNX | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131112e9bc000zo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
