\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  weaker, Czech crown drops after inflation data\b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2013\par 15:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  cbank, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Czech CPI fell more than expected, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fears loom\par     * Hungarian cbank minutes show room for further rate cuts\par     BUDAPEST/BUCHAREST, Oct 9 (Reuters) - The Czech crown led\par losses among emerging European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday after\par lower-than-expected inflation data raised the likelihood that\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Czech inflation ran at annual rate of 1.0 percent in\par September and consumer prices fell 0.4 percent month-on-month, a\par bigger drop than analysts had expected. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the data pointed to stronger downside\par risks to its inflation outlook. With interest rates already\par close to zero policymakers have been mulling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par weaken the crown as a way to help lift inflation back to the\par bank's target.  \par     "(The crown's weakening) was an immediate reaction to the\par inflation data," said Ivo Prokop, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer at Raiffeisenbank.\par     "Should it get confirmed (by future numbers) that the\par inflation trend will be going this way, the crown will not\par appreciate, as everyone will be afraid of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     By 1250 GMT, the crown was down 0.5 percent versus\par the euro at 26.6, extending losses from earlier in the session\par and hitting a one-week low. On Tuesday, it had touched a\par four-month high of 25.485.\par     The Polish zloty and the Hungarian forint\par  were each down 0.1 percent to the euro.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  minutes released on Wednesday showed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that all but one of the rate setters voted to cut the benchmark interest rate by 20 basis points last month to a record low of 3.6 percent and that further cuts might follow. In Poland, Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Tusk\f28 \uc2 \f2  denied he was planning to dismiss Finance Minister Jacek Rostowski. The Romanian leu was down 0.5 percent at 4.465 per euro, its weakest level since Sept. 30. "We see this ... as a retrenchment from the leu's stronger gains after the (U.S. Federal Reserve) decision in mid- September (not to withdraw stimulus), which we warned were vulnerable to a correction since they also occurred in such small volumes," ING said in a note. The leu could benefit from strong appetite for Romanian short-term debt, ING said, with a three-year treasury bond tender scheduled on Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   CEE MARKETS SNAPSHOT AT 1504 CET\par  ************************** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ************************\par                              Latest  Previous   Daily   Change\par                              bid     close      change  in 2013\par  Czech crown                 25.604    25.486   -0.46%  -2.17%\par  Hungarian forint           295.400   295.590  +0.06%  -1.50%\par  Polish zloty                 4.194     4.192    -0.05%  -2.86%\par  Romanian leu                 4.464     4.441   -0.52%   -0.47%\par  Croati