\par\par \b \uc2 CEE Morning Briefing: Czechs May Launch  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 835 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2013\par 03:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 0930/0730 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Inflation Report \par 1300/1100 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monetary policy decision \par 1430/1230 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  press briefing \par 1430/1230 Hungary Econ Minister Varga at conference \par 1500/1300 Hungary PM Orban at corporate event \par N/A Bulgarian parliament may hold no-confidence vote in govt \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monetary policy remains the central theme in central Europe Thursday, as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may vote to launch a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to loosen monetary conditions, hot on the heels of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slashing interest rates this week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 In Prague analysts expect no change to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark interest rate, which is at a historic low of 0.05%.\par \par \uc2 But if the monetary policy board deems it necessary to ease monetary conditions in the country that is emerging from recession, it will come via large-scale koruna sales.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is [now] the closest [it's been] to start \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a year of contemplation," said Miroslav Plojhar, economist and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Erste Bank.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Plojhar said its a 50-50 chance the bank votes for the move. However, the bank is not obliged to hold such a vote.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board hasn't found the need to launch an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet, but governor \uc2 Miroslav Singer\uc2  recently said a koruna-sale is likely while the country's inflation rate continues to undershoot the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2% target.\par \par \uc2 That comes as the \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday cut its main rate to 3.60% from 3.80%, citing a slow economy and tame inflation as drivers.\par \par \uc2 In Sofia, Bulgaria's parliament has its last chance to hold a no-confidence vote in the left-leaning, Socialist Party-led coalition.\par \par \uc2 Opposition party Citizens for European Development of Bulgaria, or GERB, put forth the motion.\par \par \uc2 However, the party's lawmakers skipped a chance to hold the vote on Wednesday and it remains likely that GERB members will again fail to register in parliament for the vote Thursday, the last day the motion can be brought to a vote.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0150 GMT 25.832-94 \par Previous 2150 GMT 25.817-90 \par %Chg +0.04 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0150 GMT 299.08-94 \par Previous 2150 GMT 299.40-300 \par % Chg -0.07 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0150 GMT 4.2182-242 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.2131-223 \par % Chg +0.08 \par  \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par          Wed    Tues \par 3 yrs    4.49%  4.52% \par 5 yrs    4.96%  4.98% \par 10yrs    5.72%  5.75% \par  \par Poland \par          Wed    Tues \par 3 yrs    3.19%  3.18%(1) \par 5 yrs    3.72%  3.66% \par 10yrs    4.35%  4.32% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par          Wed    Tues \par 3 yrs    0.39%  0.39% \par 5 yrs    1.11%  1.12% \par 10yrs    2.35%  2.35%(1) \par (1) 11 yrs \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par 2,407.12 +14.06 +0.59% \par  \par  \par BUX \par 18,687.49 +298.17 +1.62% \par  \par  \par PX \par 960.25 -1.77 -0.18% \par  \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's economic recovery isn't under threat with most recent data confirming the belief that gradual expansion continues, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Marek Belka said Wednesday night.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Belka added interest rates will remain unchanged until end of 2013 with no signs of inflation pressures in the economy, and the council will likely provide guidance early next year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Polish Airlines SA was forced to ground its \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boeing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (BA) 787 Dreamliners again when it discovered that low-pressure fuel filters were missing in engines of two planes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The troubled flag-carrier blamed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boeing\f28 \uc2 \f2  for the fault in a statement Wednesday. It said filters were missing in both engines of one aircraft and in one engine of another. It didn't say when the glitch was detected.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The Czech economy may shrink less than expected this year, and looks set to grow more than forecast in 2014 as a recovery at home and across Europe takes hold, the finance ministry said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In an unplanned update to its macroeconomic projections, the ministry now expects gross domestic product to contract 1.1% this year, less than its earlier forecast for a decline of 1.5%, and sees stronger growth of 1.3% next year, up from 0.8%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary's Export-Import Bank Zrt.'s Tuesday issuance of 400 million euros ($540 million) worth of bonds, took place at an interest level of 2.125%, Eximbank said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The issuance was guaranteed by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Multilateral Investment Guarantee Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which is part of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Group. The guarantee helped secure a triple-A rating for 95% of the bonds with rating firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/}}}\uc2 \f2  for the WSJ blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 26-09-13 0157GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020130926e99q00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
