\par\par \b \uc2 CEE Morning Briefing: Czechs May Launch  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- WSJ Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2013\par 11:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's Emerging Europe blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Sean Carney\par \par \uc2 TODAY'S CALENDAR\par \par \uc2 Local/GMT\par \par \uc2 1300/1100 \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary policy decision\par \par \uc2 1430/1230 \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  press briefing\par \par \uc2 1430/1230 Hungary Econ Minister Varga at conference\par \par \uc2 1500/1300 Hungary PM Orban at corporate event\par \par \uc2 Monetary policy remains the central theme in central Europe Thursday, as the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may vote to launch a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to loosen monetary conditions, hot on the heels of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashing interest rates and saying more easing is in the cards.\par \par \uc2 In Prague analysts expect no change to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark interest rate, which is at a historic low of 0.05%.\par \par \uc2 But if the monetary policy board deems it necessary to ease monetary conditions in the country that is emerging from recession, it will come via large-scale koruna sales.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is [now] the closest [it's been] to start \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a year of contemplation," said Miroslav Plojhar, economist and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Erste Bank.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Plojhar said its a 50-50 chance the bank votes for the move. However, the bank is not obliged to hold such a vote.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board hasn't found the need to launch an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet, but governor \uc2 Miroslav Singer\uc2  recently said a koruna-sale is likely while the country's inflation rate continues to undershoot the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2% target.\par \par \uc2 That comes as the \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday cut its main rate to 3.60% from 3.80%, citing a slow economy and tame inflation as drivers.\par \par \uc2 Then on Thursday the \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its quarterly Inflation Report said it sees room for further moderate monetary easing as it expects domestic inflationary pressures to remain muted through the end of next year.\par \par \uc2 In Sofia, Bulgaria's parliament earlier in the day had its last chance to hold a no-confidence vote in the left-leaning, Socialist Party-led coalition, and the motion failed to come to vote due to a lack of quorum.\par \par \uc2 Opposition party Citizens for European Development of Bulgaria, or GERB, put forth the motion but left the chamber before a vote could be called as they would have lacked a majority in the 240-seat parliament to push the government out of power.\par \par \uc2 OTHER NEWS\par \par \uc2 POLAND: Poland's economic recovery isn't under threat with most recent data confirming the belief that gradual expansion continues, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Marek Belka said Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Belka added interest rates will remain unchanged until end of 2013 with no signs of inflation pressures in the economy, and the council will likely provide guidance early next year.\par \par \uc2 POLAND: Polish Airlines SA was forced to ground its \uc2 Boeing Co\uc2 . (BA) 787 Dreamliners again when it discovered that low-pressure fuel filters were missing in engines of two planes.\par \par \uc2 The troubled flag-carrier blamed \uc2 Boeing\uc2  for the fault in a statement Wednesday. It said filters were missing in both engines of one aircraft and in one engine of another. It didn't say when the glitch was detected.\par \par \uc2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The Czech economy may shrink less than expected this year, and looks set to grow more than forecast in 2014 as a recovery at home and across Europe takes hold, the finance ministry said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In an unplanned update to its macroeconomic projections, the ministry now expects gross domestic product to contract 1.1% this year, less than its earlier forecast for a decline of 1.5%, and sees stronger growth of 1.3% next year, up from 0.8%.\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY: Hungary's Export-Import Bank Zrt.'s Tuesday issuance of 400 million euros ($540 million) worth of bonds, took place at an interest level of 2.125%, Eximbank said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The issuance was guaranteed by the \uc2 Multilateral Investment Guarantee Agency\uc2 , which is part of the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  Group. The guarantee helped secure a triple-A rating for 95% of the bonds with rating firm \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 26-09-13 0924GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130926e99q000cm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
