\par\par \b \uc2 CEE Morning Briefing: Czechs May Launch  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 835 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2013\par 03:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 0930/0730 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Inflation Report \par 1300/1100 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monetary policy decision \par 1430/1230 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  press briefing \par 1430/1230 Hungary Econ Minister Varga at conference \par 1500/1300 Hungary PM Orban at corporate event \par N/A Bulgarian parliament may hold no-confidence vote in govt \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monetary policy remains the central theme in central Europe Thursday, as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may vote to launch a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to loosen monetary conditions, hot on the heels of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slashing interest rates this week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 In Prague analysts expect no change to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark interest rate, which is at a historic low of 0.05%.\par \par \uc2 But if the monetary policy board deems it necessary to ease monetary conditions in the country that is emerging from recession, it will come via large-scale koruna sales.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is [now] the closest [it's been] to start \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a year of contemplation," said Miroslav Plojhar, economist and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Erste Bank.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Plojhar said its a 50-50 chance the bank votes for the move. However, the bank is not obliged to hold such a vote.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board hasn't found the need to launch an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet, but governor \uc2 Miroslav Singer\uc2  recently said a koruna-sale is likely while the country's inflation rate continues to undershoot the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2% target.\par \par \uc2 That comes as the \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday cut its main rate to 3.60% from 3.80%, citing a slow economy and tame inflation as drivers.\par \par \uc2 In Sofia, Bulgaria's parliament has its last chance to hold a no-confidence vote in the left-leaning, Socialist Party-led coalition.\par \par \uc2 Opposition party Citizens for European Development of Bulgaria, or GERB, put forth the motion.\par \par \uc2 However, the party's lawmakers skipped a chance to hold the vote on Wednesday and it remains likely that GERB members will again fail to register in parliament for the vote Thursday, the last day the motion can be brought to a vote.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0150 GMT 25.832-94 \par Previous 2150 GMT 25.817-90 \par %Chg +0.04 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0150 GMT 299.08-94 \par Previous 2150 GMT 299.40-300 \par % Chg -0.07 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0150 GMT 4.2182-242 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.2131-223 \par % Chg +0.08 \par  \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par          Wed    Tues \par 3 yrs    4.49%  4.52% \par 5 yrs    4.96%  4.98% \par 10yrs    5.72%  5.75% \par  \par Poland \par          Wed    Tues \par 3 yrs    3.19%  3.18%(1) \par 5 yrs    3.72%  3.66% \par 10yrs    4.35%  4.32% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par          Wed    Tues \par 