\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2-Hungary's OTP shares plunge, Czech crown steady\b0\par\par\uc2 812 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2013\par 17:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with Hungary, adds yields, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 OTP Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares fall 5 pct, drag on forint; yields rise\par     * Budapest govt to start talks with banks on new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loan\par plan\par     * Crown steady ahead of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     BUCHAREST, July 29 (Reuters) - Shares in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's biggest\par lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 OTP Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  plunged again on Monday, hurt by government\par plans to rewrite foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mortgages which also pushed\par debt yields higher and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower.\par     The fall of more than 5 percent came after OTP said board\par member Peter Braoun had sold 200,000 shares in the bank on\par Friday at an average price of 4,555 forints ($20.28) per share,\par following a share sale earlier in July by its chief executive.\par     The government in Budapest, which faces an election next\par year, unnerved markets this month when it said it wanted to\par phase out foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mortgages, seeking to help struggling\par households but hurting banks in the process. \par     Since Hungary's government announced its mortgage plan on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 16, OTP shares have fallen by roughly 17 percent, wiping about 200 billion forints ($890.64 million) off the bank's market capitalization. The bank took another hit when its chairman and CEO sold a big chunk of shares to finance his agricultural business. At 1405 GMT, OTP shares were down 5.1 percent from the previous session at 4,307 forints, helping knock Budapest's blue-chip index down 2 percent. "It is driven by uncertainty over what exactly the government plans to do with foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mortgages," an equity trader said. The falls may also have been magnified by low summer trading volumes. The forint was down 0.5 percent on the day at 298.4, while 10-year bond yields rose 17 basis points.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     CZECH CBANK MEETING\par     Elsewhere in the region, the Polish zloty was 0.3\par percent stronger against the euro, while the Romanian leu\par  fell 0.1 percent.\par     The Czech crown was up 0.1 percent ahead of a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting later this week at which policymakers will\par discuss possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Having cut interest rates to near zero, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been debating whether to take further action to help\par the economy, which has not grown in two years.\par     But all 16 analysts polled by Reuters last week expect the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bank to decide against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when it meets on Thursday as it has succeeded so far in talking the crown down. A minority of policymakers strongly support doing more to weaken the crown. "The probability of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has increased, even if the potential effects of a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on domestic and foreign demand are ambiguous," \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a research note. It said the cost to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's credibility could be significant if it focused excessively on the exchange rate. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   CEE MARKETS SNAPSHOT AT 1722 CET\par  ************************** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ************************\par                              Latest  Previous   Daily   Change\par                              bid     close      change  in 2013\par  Czech crown                 25.865    25.907  +0.16%  -3.16%\par  Hungarian forint           298.560   297.100   -0.49%  -2.55%\par  Polish zloty                 4.216     4.228   +0.28%  -3.37%\par  Romanian leu                 4.393     4.388   -0.11%  +1.14%\par  Croatian kuna                7.503     7.502    -0.02% +0.64%\par  Serbian dinar              113.660   113.880   +0.19%   -1.20%\par  Note: daily change calculated from previous close at 1600 GMT\par  **************************** STOCKS **************************\par                              Latest  Previous   Daily   Change\par                                      close      change  in 2013\par  Prague                      912.07    912.45   -0.04%  -12.19%\par  Budapest                  18087.02  18467.76    -2.06%   -0.47%\par  Warsaw                     2287.57   2291.10    -0.15%  -11.44%\par  Bucharest                  5383.23   5380.97  +0.04%  +4.54%\par  ***************************** BONDS **************************\par                          Yield    Yield    Spread    Daily\par                          (bid)    change   vs Bund   change in\par  Czech Republic                                      spread\par    2-year                0.498    -0.004   +34bps     -1bps\par    5-year                1.474     -0.020   +81bps      -3bps\par   10-year                2.187    -0.007   +51bps     -2b