\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2-Forint gains on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  loan plan, crown lags\b0\par\par\uc2 785 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2013\par 15:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll, Polish news on deficit rules)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Forint up as Orban says doesn't plan "Blitzkrieg" on banks\par     * Budapest's new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loan push has weighed on assets\par     * Crown weak on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk\par     WARSAW/PRAGUE, July 26 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's forint led\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 gains in central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, lifted by optimism over the government's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan plan, while the Czech crown weakened ahead of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting next weak. Hungary's Prime Minister Victor Orban said he aimed to resolve the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mortgage problem without wrecking the financial system. The forint was up by 0.35 percent to 296.68 against the euro by 1311 GMT, easing slightly from the day's high of 295.94, and recovering from a one-month low of 298.1 hit on Thursday in shallow trade. "Concerns about the programme to help \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowers have to a certain extent abated and the forint has somewhat rebounded due to that," a Budapest-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. The market reacted nervously after the cabinet issued a statement on Wednesday saying it planned to talk to banks about a solution to help the many Hungarian households who took out foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans when the forint was stronger and are now struggling to repay them. Orban's administration has passed a swathe of controversial laws since coming to power three years ago that have unnerved investors, including nationalising pension assets and imposing the highest tax on banks in Europe. The Czech crown eased 0.17 percent to 25.934 a euro ahead of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy meeting next Thursday at which policymakers are seen discussing whether to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  now that interest rates are effectively at zero. All 16 analysts who responded to questions on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a Reuters poll said the bank would hold fire but the board is split and minutes from the previous session in June showed several bankers called for immediately launching crown sales. News on Thursday that all board member would attend the meeting mean it could be more difficult for the dovish camp on the board to push through sales of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. The Czech economy is trapped in almost a two-year long recession hit by austerity measures and weak demand for its exports. Some policymakers are concerned a recovery expected in the latter half of 2013 is not materialising. Elsewhere, the Polish zloty, the region's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , inched up 0.17 percent to 4.238, but the move was well within Thursday's trading range. The zloty shrugged off news that parliament has approved a draft bill allowing for higher deficits to aid the sharply slowing economy. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                    CEE MARKETS SNAPSHOT AT 1514 CET\par  ************************** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ************************\par                             