\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-China leads stocks lower,  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  loan plan rattles Hungarian assets\b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2013\par 13:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, July 19 (Reuters) - Emerging market equities dipped on Friday, led by losses in Chinese property and financial stocks while Hungarian shares fell sharply on concern about government plans to modify the terms of private foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets have begun to stabilise after weeks of outflows and losses suffered on concern about an end to the U.S. monetary stimulus which has boosted demand for high-yielding assets.\par \par \uc2 In a much anticipated speech to Congress on Thursday, Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  said it was too soon to make a call on dialling back quantitative easing in September.\par \par \uc2 Despite Friday's losses, stocks were heading for their second week of gains.\par \par \uc2 "We are in a strong dollar but low interest rates environment which will take some pressure off from emerging markets in the short term and we have indeed seen a bit of index recovery but the issues around China and corporate governance mean we probably have more underperformance to come," said John-Paul Smith, global emerging equities analyst at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chinese stocks fell for a third straight day due to declines in financial and property firms.\par \par \uc2 After the market close China announced it was relaxing controls on bank deposit rates, part of long-awaited interest rate reforms.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely stepped in via state-run banks again, dealers said, to prop up the rupee, which has fallen back to levels seen before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved on Monday to drain liquidity and push up short-term interest rates to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A government bond auction on Friday would be a key test of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, with investors betting the sale would be a struggle.\par \par \uc2 Emerging equities dropped 0.5 percent, with Hungarian stocks falling more than 2 percent to their lowest in more than two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's OTP Bank Chief Executive Sandor Csanyi sold a big chunk of his shares in the bank on Thursday, driving OTP shares lower after two days of steep falls on government plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan contracts.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint hit two-week lows against the euro .\par \par \uc2 Emerging market debt spreads widened by 1 basis point to 321 bps over U.S. Treasuries. Emerging debt spreads have been tightening in recent days after widening as much as 100 bps in June.\par \par \uc2 In the week leading to July 17, emerging market outflows continued. Equity funds saw $0.04 billion in outflows, while bond funds suffered $1.3 billion of outflows, according to banks citing EPFR data.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Philip Baillie and Sujata Rao; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING | BX | CZS | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | Z | SNI | SNS | HX | PX | RDN | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130722e97j000hh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
