\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2-Czech crown eases before cbank meets, forint firms\b0\par\par\uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 17:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Crown eases on renewed worry that cbank could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Forint extends gain as cbank did not announce radical measures\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Sandor Peto\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE/BUDAPEST, March 27 (Reuters) - The Czech crown lost ground on Wednesday amid some worries before Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting that the bank could give new signals of market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint firmed, going against the direction of other assets in the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's emerging markets which fell as the euro was knocked by Italy's disappointing bond auction and bailout plans for Cyprus.\par \par \uc2 Central European equity markets were lower, led by Bucharest's main stock index .BETI> which dropped 1.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bonds were resilient after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained on Tuesday from radical easing measures that had been anticipated by some investors.\par \par \uc2 The forint extended gains posted after Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting, at which the bank cut its base rate by a quarter point to a record low of 5 percent. It was bid at 303.65 to the euro at 1537 GMT, 0.2 percent firmer from Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "Positioning helps the forint," one Budapest-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said.\par \par \uc2 "Some investors had expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to announce some unorthodox ideas (to help the recession-hit economy), and that has not happened, and the statement was quite moderate," the dealer said, projecting a 303-305 range for the next days.\par \par \uc2 Early this month Prime Minister Viktor Orban picked close ally and former Economy Minister Gyorgy Matolcsy to head the bank with a mandate to help the economy, sparking fears the bank\par \par \uc2 may implement unconventional measures that would hit the forint.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in the region have been cutting their interest rates in the past year to help economies hit by economic slowdown in their main export markets in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 With Czech interest rates already at "technical zero", the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  there has said \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be its next easing tool to help the contracting economy.\par \par \uc2 The weakening of the crown to a nine-month low in the past month reduced those chances, but concerns ahead of Thursday's policy meeting weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again.\par \par \uc2 It eased by 0.1 percent to 25.75 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 "We still see global names buying EUR/CZK from 25.700 up to now. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be one reason for nerves," one Prague-based dealer said. "We are also going into the Easter holiday weekend."\par \par \uc2 Market participants said the crown could rebound, just as it did after the bank's meeting last month, if the bank does not give clear signals of market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Poland's zloty was flat at 4.181 against the euro, while Romania's leu eased 0.2 percent to 4.417.\par \par \uc2 All three of central Europe's bigger former communist economies have been cutting rates steadily in a bid to bolster growth as most of the euro zone falters.\par \par \uc2 Only Romania, which meets on Thursday, has stayed on hold due to inflation pressures. Analysts do not expect loosening there until later in 2013.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2013 \par Czech crown                  25.75    25.731   -0.07%    -2.73%\par Polish zloty                 4.181    4.18   -0.02%    -2.56%\par Hungarian forint             303.65    304.33  +0.22%    -4.18%\par Croatian kuna                7.594    7.592   -0.03%    -0.57%\par Romanian leu                 4.417    4.408   -0.2%   +0.59%\par Serbian dinar                111.95    111.67   -0.25%   +0.31%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR    0 basis points to  45bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR   +5 basis points to  +97bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ9YT=RR   +7 basis points to  +126bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds           \par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +507bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR   +8 basis points to  +531bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR +8 basis points to  +499bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All data taken from Reuters at 1637 CET.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  percent change calculated from the daily domestic\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 close at 1700 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For related news and prices, click on the codes in brackets: All emerging market news Spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Eastern Europe spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highligh