\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2-Hungarian forint slips after rate cut\b0\par\par\uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2013\par 16:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds Hungarian rates, Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  cuts rates 25 bps, market awaits new cbank head\par \par \uc2 * Italy vote knocks other regional assets\par \par \uc2 * Crown eases after cbanker says more easing may be needed\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Goettig and Sam Cage\par \par \uc2 WARSAW/SOFIA, Feb 26 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint slipped on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates for the seventh meeting running, ahead of the appointment of a new governor expected to further expand stimulus for the economy.\par \par \uc2 An inconclusive Italian election result that hit the euro and a raft of European stock and bond markets, put broad pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the developing economies of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's eastern wing.\par \par \uc2 Hungary, the region's most-indebted economy, has now hacked 175 basis points off base interest rates since August, when the divided Monetary Council began an easing cycle to aid the recession-hit economy.\par \par \uc2 Hit by expectations the bank will do more, and worries over a policy mix which has put off international investors, the forint has shed more than 1 percent so far this year. It was bid 0.2 percent lower at 294.65 per euro by 1500 GMT.\par \par \uc2 "We would not be surprised to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening past 300 in the coming weeks," said Equilor analyst Gergely Gabler in Budapest.\par \par \uc2 The cut to 5.25 percent - a record low - had been largely priced in and markets already expect the premium for holding the forint to be cut to about 4.5 percent. But there is lingering concern that riskier monetary policy measures cooked up in government workshops could hit the forint if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implements them.\par \par \uc2 The forint has been stable at 290-295 in recent weeks, but previously it fell on fears that the bank could limit commercial banks' access to its two-week bills, the main tool that drains liquidity from interbank markets.\par \par \uc2 Regional stock markets followed western European peers sharply lower, with the Budapest bourse leading losses with a 1.8 percent fall. Poland's zloty was the biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  loser, dropping 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Dealers all blamed the turnaround in expectations for the Italian elections from more positive initial polls on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "The market is on a roller-coaster," said Bartlomiej Rostek, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at \uc2 ING Bank Slaski\uc2 . "Yesterday it seemed that we are in for further zloty gains and now we have a complete risk-off."\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown dipped to a day's low of 25.58 per euro after a board member said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may still need to ease monetary policy further and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be the likely way to go. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later recovered some ground and was 0.2 percent lower on the day.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2013 \par Czech cro