\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  gain after EU clinches budget deal\b0\par\par\uc2 922 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2013\par 17:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates throughout)\par \par \uc2 * Deal means more EU funds to support region's investment\par \par \uc2 * CZK near 1-mth high as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk seen lower\par \par \uc2 * Broad euro weakness also supports CEE \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Sam Cage and Marcin Goettig\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST/WARSAW, Feb 8 (Reuters) - Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained on Friday, lifted by news that European leaders had reached a deal on the long-term budget, and the Czech crown hovered near a one-month high after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sounded softer on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stock markets were mixed, with \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main stock index\par \par \uc2 dragged lower by a more than 4 percent drop in oil and gas group MOL after an Abu Dhabi energy firm sold shares.\par \par \uc2 There was relief that EU leaders had struck a budget deal as countries in central Europe rely on \uc2 European Union\uc2  structural funds to support public investments in infrastructure like roads, bridges and airports.\par \par \uc2 An impasse on the EU budget could stall the long-term investments, needed to spur growth in the region's weak economies.\par \par \uc2 Poland is the largest recipient of the funds, which have helped it avoid recession since 2008, the only country in the \uc2 European Union\uc2  to do so.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained somewhat after the news about the deal," said a Warsaw-based dealer.\par \par \uc2 The zloty gained 0.3 percent to 4.15 versus the euro by 1551 GMT. Hungary's forint rose 0.7 percent, while the Romanian leu added 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said that a temporary reversal of the usual correlation between the euro/dollar rate and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could provide further support for the zloty.\par \par \uc2 "We are in an interesting period when the EUR/PLN rate is moving in lock step with the EUR/USD rate," said Miroslaw Budzicki, a strategist at Poland's largest lender PKO BP.\par \par \uc2 Most often a fall in the euro versus the dollar, usually driven by higher risk aversion, means losses for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 But currently the 30-day correlation between the EUR/PLN and the EUR/USD was the highest in 22 months, Reuters data showed, inverting the usual relationship.\par \par \uc2 Budzicki said that a likely continuation of the euro's slide, which was triggered by comments from ECB chief \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  on Thursday, meant that the zloty could gain more in the short term.\par \par \uc2 Draghi's comments that the exchange rate was important for growth and price stability were perceived by investors as a sign the bank could be willing to cut interest rates if euro appreciation continues.\par \par \uc2 "Additionally Polish rate cut expectations have been scaled back," Budzicki added.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped the wording on further possible "monetary easing" from its statement after it cut rates on Wednesday for a fourth successive month, signaling that a pause in the easing cycle may be near.\par \par \uc2 CROWN FIRMS\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown rose 0.1 percent to 25.23 per euro, close to a one-month high hit the previous day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked "less urgent".\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could tolerate some strengthening but any strong firming beyond 25.20 or 25.00 could prompt it to step into the market to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Polish bonds were stable, while their Hungarian counterparts gained following the forint's gains.\par \par \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  analysts recommended buying the Romanian leu, after its slide over the last three weeks from a one-year high against the euro hit in mid-January. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was flat on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2013 \par Czech crown                  25.229  25.262   +0.13%    -0.72%\par Polish zloty                 4.15    4.176    +0.63%    -1.83%\par Hungarian forint             290.8   292.75   +0.67%    +0.06%Croatian kuna                7.578   7.578     0%       -0.36%\par Romanian leu                 4.394   4.397    +0.07%    +1.12%\par Serbian dinar                111.78  111.64   -0.13%    +0.47%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR    -1 basis points to  8bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR    -2 basis points to  +55bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ9YT=RR   +1 basis points to  +111bps over bmk*\par Polish treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   PL2YT=RR   +1 basis points to  +316bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   PL5YT=RR    -1 basis points to  +290bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond PL10YT=RR    0 basis p