\par\par \b \uc2 DJ PMIs in Focus in First Week of New Year in Central Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2012\par 17:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (This item will be published next Jan. 4, 2013.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Veronika Gulyas and Sean Carney \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST--Little macroeconomic data are scheduled for release in central Europe after Christmas and before New Year's Eve, but purchasing managers indexes for the manufacturing sector will be watched closely by investors in the first week of 2013.\par \par \uc2 PMI figures have been below the threshold level of 50 in Poland, the Czech republic and Hungary in recent months, indicating a contraction in activity, mainly a result of a slowing euro-zone economic growth.\par \par \uc2 In Prague, on the last day of 2012, the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release minutes from its Dec. 19 monetary policy meeting, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unanimously voted to keep interest rates at historic lows, with the benchmark rate at 0.05%. After the rate decision, the bank's governor, Miroslav Singer, said monetary policy easing was likely to take place in mid-2013 through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account is expected to post a large surplus in the third quarter, up significantly from the previous quarter.\par \par \uc2 "The positive current-account balance is favorable for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the interest differential has been melting away since the summer, and thus the forint cannot really benefit from the improving external sentiment," Erste Bank economist Zoltan Arokszallasi said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Date   GMT  Country Indicator   Period Forecast    Previous \par Dec 24 N/A  Markets closed for holiday \par Dec 25 N/A  Markets closed for holiday \par Dec 26 N/A  Markets closed for holiday \par Dec 27 0800 CZE Confidence Index Dec   N/A         82.2 \par Dec 28 0730 HUN Curr Acct       3Q     +EUR689M(3) +EUR519M \par Dec 31 0800 CZE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  minutes from Dec 19 meeting \par Dec 31 N/A  HUN Markets closed for holiday \par Jan 02 N/A  CZE PMI             Dec    N/A         48.2 \par Jan 02 0800 POL PMI             Dec    N/A         48.2 \par Jan 02 N/A  CZE Budget balance  Dec    N/A         -CZK77.87B \par Jan 02 N/A  HUN PMI             Dec    N/A         52.3 \par Jan 02 1030 HUN 3-Month T-Bill  Tender N/A         5.63%* \par Jan 04 0800 HUN Jobless         SepNov 11%(2)      10.5% \par Notes: \par    Numbers in brackets indicate the number of analysts polled by Dow Jones Newswires. \par    N/A indicates "not available" or "not applicable." Some amounts denoted as previous are rounded. \par    *   - Average auction yield. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Patryk Wasilewski in Warsaw contributed to this item.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Veronika Gulyas at veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 21, 2012 11:28 ET (16:28 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121221e8cl00548\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
