\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Minutes from Hungary's Rate-cut Meeting Due\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2012\par 03:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 1200/1400 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  minutes \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday will publish the minutes of its September rate-settting meeting at which the monetary policy board surprised markets and eased monetary policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Ahead of the vote, analysts mostly expected no change to policy, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made its second consecutive 25 basis-points interest-rate cut that brought the benchmark rate to 6.50%.\par \par \uc2 Rate setters have already revealed that the vote, just as the previous vote in August, passed by a four to three majority. In the previous vote, the newer, dovish members outvoted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor and his two deputies who then opted to keep the rate unchanged.\par \par \uc2 The minutes can nonetheless provide further indication about the short-term outlook for monetary policy in Hungary and may show whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  will join the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on markets to ease recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0150 GMT 24.955-5.006 \par Previous 2150 GMT 24.937-5.015 \par %Chg  +0.02 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0150 GMT 282.62-4.12 \par Previous 2150 GMT  283.01-76 \par % Chg  -0.01 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0150 GMT 4.0737-804 \par Previous 2150 GMT  4.0698-783 \par % Chg   +0.07 \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par         Tues    Mon \par 3 yrs   6.55%   6.53% \par 5 yrs   6.65%   6.65% \par 10yrs   7.13%   7.15% \par  \par Poland \par         Tues    Mon \par 3 yrs   4.02%   4.01%(1) \par 5 yrs   4.20%   4.17% \par 10yrs   4.65%   4.65% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par         Tues    Mon \par 3 yrs   0.57%   0.57% \par 5 yrs   1.13%   1.13% \par 10yrs   2.28%   2.28% \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par 2,376.24-24.75-1.03% \par  \par BUX \par 18,865.10-101.15-0.53% \par  \par PX \par 985.96+0.44+0.04% \par  \par EU Enlarged \par 1,966.15-18.40-0.93% \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Polish and Slovak authorities Tuesday canceled their nation's respective bans on imports and sales of hard alcohol from the Czech Republic, according to news reports in both countries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary's right-wing Prime Minister Viktor Orban voiced concern Tuesday about what he said was increasing nationalism in neighbouring Romania, in comments set to raise tensions during Romanian elections in December.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: A Romanian High Court judge was sentenced Tuesday to four years in prison on corruption charges, a judicial sources said. Maria David was accused of receiving more than 200,000 euros ($258,000) in bribes in 2009 from a businessman found guilty of tax fraud. She promised to speak up for him at an appeals court.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BULGARIA: Support for Bulgaria's centre-right government and Prime Minister Boyko Borisov plunged between June and September, a new opinion poll showed Tuesday, nine months before elections are due. Forty-five percent of the 1,012 people polled by the Alpha Research Institute in September said they disapproved of the government, with only 18 percent still staunchly supporting it.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Gergo Racz in Budapest contributed to this briefing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sean Carney\f28 \uc2 \f2  at sean.carney@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 10-10-12 0158GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020121010e8aa00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
