\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Czech, Hungarian 1Q GDP Details Due\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2012\par 04:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 0700/0900 Hungary April foreign trade data \par 0700/0900 Hungary first quarter final GDP data \par 0700/0900 Czech first quarter final GDP data \par 0700/0900 Czech unemployment in May \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Final readings of first quarter gross domestic product data in the Czech Republic and Hungary are due Friday, along with Czech May jobless reading and Hungary's foreign trade balance in April.\f28 \par \par \uc2 In Prague, the revised GDP reading is expected to be little changed from the preliminary first-quarter reading, which came in worse-than-expected with contractions of 1% in both annual and quarterly terms.\par \par \uc2 Dalimil Vyskovsky, a fixed-income trader at \uc2 Komercni Banka\uc2  in Prague, said the sharp decline in the flash reading was puzzling and said the bond market will be closely watching Friday for any revisions.\par \par \uc2 The economic growth data is likely to play a larger-than-normal role in the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy decision later this month, Mr. Vyskovsky said.\par \par \uc2 Any upswing in Czech May unemployment, which is expected at 8.2% from April's 8.4%, will add to pressure for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut interest rates on June 28, which would be the first change to monetary policy in more than two years, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 In Budapest, investors are eying Hungary's detailed gross domestic product data to capture which factor pulled Hungary's economy into recession in early 2012.\par \par \uc2 Preliminary GDP data showed a 0.7% contraction in unadjusted terms, mainly due to a plunge in construction in February and March, as well as on further declining consumption and investments, Takarekbank said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0150 GMT 25.256-86 \par Previous 2150 GMT 25.313-71 \par %Chg -0.28 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0150 GMT 295.81-6.50 \par Previous 2150 GMT 294.88-5.67 \par % Chg  +0.30 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0150 GMT 4.2748-94 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.2637-716 \par % Chg  +0.22 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par         Thurs  Wed \par 3 yrs   8.15%  8.35% \par 5 yrs   8.20%  8.50% \par 10yrs   8.25%  8.60% \par  \par Poland \par         Thurs  Wed \par 3 yrs   4.74%  4.74%(1) \par 5 yrs   4.85%  4.85% \par 10yrs   5.31%  5.31% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par         Thurs  Wed \par 3 yrs   1.09%  1.10% \par 5 yrs   1.94%  1.94% \par 10yrs   3.16%  3.16% \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par Polish markets were closed Thursday for a bank holiday \par  \par BUX \par 16,990.10+48.75+0.29% \par  \par PX \par 892.9  +11.7  +1.3% \par  \par EU Enlarged \par 1,726.58+22.66+1.33% \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's finance minister urged Thursday that EU rescue funds be used directly to recapitalise struggling Spanish banks, arguing it would be senseless to increase Spain's debt during the crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: The National Bank of Poland stands ready to prevent the zloty from weakening rapidly, the bank's governor said, although the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is less volatile now than last year, when the bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support it.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HUNGARY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's year-to-date budget deficit widened further in May on higher subsidies and increased payments at the state-owned railway firm, the national economy ministry said Thursday. The budget posted a deficit of 115.9 billion forints ($498 million) in May, about 38% of the gap allowed under the country's plans to reduce its deficit to 2.5% of gross domestic product this year, the ministry said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will probably lower its gross domestic product forecasts for this year and next, Andras Simor, the monetary policy authority's governor, was quoted as saying Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Veronika Gulyas in Budapest contributed to this briefing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 08-06-12 0206GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020120608e86800001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
