\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ BLOG/Emerging Europe: MORNING BRIEFING: Czech, Hungarian 1Q GDP Details Due\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2012\par 10:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's Emerging Europe blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 By Sean Carney\par \par \uc2 TODAY'S CALENDAR\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Local/GMT \par  \par    -- 0700/0900 Hungary April foreign trade data \par  \par    -- 0700/0900 Hungary first quarter final GDP data \par  \par    -- 0700/0900 Czech first quarter final GDP data \par  \par    -- 0700/0900 Czech unemployment in May \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Final readings of first quarter gross domestic product data in the Czech Republic and Hungary are due Friday, along with Czech May jobless reading and Hungary's foreign trade balance in April. In Prague, the revised GDP reading is expected to be little changed from the preliminary first-quarter reading, which came in worse-than-expected with contractions of 1% in both annual and quarterly terms. Dalimil Vyskovsky, a fixed-income trader at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Komercni Banka\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Prague, said the sharp decline in the flash reading was puzzling and said the bond market will be closely watching Friday for any revisions. The economic growth data is likely to play a larger-than-normal role in the Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy decision later this month, Mr. Vyskovsky said. Any upswing in Czech May unemployment, which is expected at 8.2% from April's 8.4%, will add to pressure for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut interest rates on June 28, which would be the first change to monetary policy in more than two years, analysts said. In Budapest, investors are eying Hungary's detailed gross domestic product data to capture which factor pulled Hungary's economy into recession in early 2012. Preliminary GDP data showed a 0.7% contraction in unadjusted terms, mainly due to a plunge in construction in February and March, as well as on further declining consumption and investments, Takarekbank said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OTHER NEWS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's finance minister urged Thursday that EU rescue funds be used directly to recapitalise struggling Spanish banks, arguing it would be senseless to increase Spain's debt during the crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: The National Bank of Poland stands ready to prevent the zloty from weakening rapidly, the bank's governor said, although the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is less volatile now than last year, when the bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support it.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HUNGARY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's year-to-date budget deficit widened further in May on higher subsidies and increased payments at the state-owned railway firm, the national economy ministry said Thursday. The budget posted a deficit of 115.9 billion forints ($498 million) in May, about 38% of the gap allowed under the country's plans to reduce its deficit to 2.5% of gross domestic product this year, the ministry said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will probably lower its gross domestic product forecasts for this year and next, Andras Simor, the monetary policy authority's governor, was quoted as saying Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Veronika Gulyas in Budapest contributed to this briefing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-06-12 0823GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120608e868000ok\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (hungary near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\cl